1
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:41,041
These are dark times, there is no denying.

2
00:00:41,626 --> 00:00:47,256
Our world has, perhaps,
faced no greater threat than it does today.

3
00:00:48,258 --> 00:00:52,219
But I say this to our citizenry:

4
00:00:52,387 --> 00:00:56,265
We, ever your servants...

5
00:00:56,433 --> 00:00:59,101
...will continue to defend your liberty...

6
00:00:59,269 --> 00:01:03,605
...and repel the forces
that seek to take it from you.

7
00:01:04,816 --> 00:01:10,112
Your Ministry remains...

8
00:01:10,613 --> 00:01:12,614
...strong.

9
00:01:29,966 --> 00:01:32,134
Hermione. Tea's ready, darling.

10
00:01:32,302 --> 00:01:34,261
Coming, Mom.

11
00:01:38,183 --> 00:01:40,100
Come on, Dudley, hurry up.

12
00:01:40,268 --> 00:01:43,312
I still don't understand
why we have to leave.

13
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:48,233
Because, unh,
it's not safe for us here any more.

14
00:02:03,625 --> 00:02:08,003
Ron, tell your father
supper's nearly ready.

15
00:02:13,009 --> 00:02:14,718
Is this in Australia?

16
00:02:14,886 --> 00:02:16,845
Looks wonderful, doesn't it?

17
00:02:17,013 --> 00:02:21,892
Three and a half thousand
kilometers along Australia's east coast.

18
00:02:23,186 --> 00:02:24,728
Obliviate.

19
00:04:39,072 --> 00:04:40,739
Severus.

20
00:04:40,907 --> 00:04:44,284
I was beginning to worry
you had lost your way.

21
00:04:44,452 --> 00:04:47,913
Come, we've saved you a seat.

22
00:04:52,335 --> 00:04:53,669
You bring news, I trust?

23
00:04:53,836 --> 00:04:57,506
It will happen Saturday next, at nightfall.

24
00:04:57,674 --> 00:05:00,050
I've heard differently, my Lord.

25
00:05:00,218 --> 00:05:03,345
Dawlish, the Auror,
has let slip that the Potter boy...

26
00:05:03,513 --> 00:05:06,640
...will not be moved
until the 30th of this month.

27
00:05:07,058 --> 00:05:08,350
The day before he turns 17.

28
00:05:08,518 --> 00:05:11,728
This is a false trail.

29
00:05:12,397 --> 00:05:16,566
The Auror Office no longer plays any part
in the protection of Harry Potter.

30
00:05:16,734 --> 00:05:21,113
Those closest to him believe
we have infiltrated the Ministry.

31
00:05:21,698 --> 00:05:23,323
Well, they got that right, haven't they?

32
00:05:27,787 --> 00:05:30,247
What say you, Pius?

33
00:05:33,793 --> 00:05:36,378
One hears many things, my Lord.

34
00:05:36,546 --> 00:05:39,131
Whether the truth is among them
is not clear.

35
00:05:39,298 --> 00:05:42,676
Heh. Spoken like a true politician.

36
00:05:42,844 --> 00:05:45,887
You will, I think,
prove most useful, Pius.

37
00:05:49,517 --> 00:05:52,728
- Where will he be taken, the boy?
- To a safe house.

38
00:05:53,146 --> 00:05:55,772
Most likely the home of someone
in the Order.

39
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:59,192
I'm told it's been given
every manner of protection possible.

40
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:02,946
Once there,
it will be impractical to attack him.

41
00:06:03,531 --> 00:06:08,076
Ahem. My Lord.
I'd like to volunteer myself for this task.

42
00:06:08,244 --> 00:06:09,244
I want to kill the boy.

43
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:11,788
Wormtail!

44
00:06:11,956 --> 00:06:14,875
Have I not spoken to you
about keeping our guest quiet?

45
00:06:15,126 --> 00:06:17,002
Yes, my Lord.

46
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:19,838
Right away, my Lord.

47
00:06:20,089 --> 00:06:24,593
As inspiring
as I find your bloodlust, Bellatrix...

48
00:06:25,011 --> 00:06:28,305
...I must be the one to kill Harry Potter.

49
00:06:30,767 --> 00:06:35,604
But I face an unfortunate complication.

50
00:06:35,772 --> 00:06:40,942
That my wand and Potter's
share the same core.

51
00:06:42,195 --> 00:06:48,784
They are, in some ways, twins.

52
00:06:48,951 --> 00:06:53,622
We can wound,
but not fatally harm one another.

53
00:06:55,249 --> 00:06:58,043
If I am to kill him...

54
00:06:58,711 --> 00:07:02,464
...I must do it with another's wand.

55
00:07:04,467 --> 00:07:10,180
Come, surely one of you
would like the honor?

56
00:07:11,808 --> 00:07:13,475
Mm?

57
00:07:15,144 --> 00:07:19,981
What about you, Lucius?

58
00:07:22,485 --> 00:07:23,860
My Lord?

59
00:07:24,028 --> 00:07:25,987
"My Lord?"

60
00:07:27,073 --> 00:07:30,700
I require your wand.

61
00:07:44,006 --> 00:07:46,508
Do I detect elm?

62
00:07:46,676 --> 00:07:48,635
Yes, my Lord.

63
00:07:54,559 --> 00:07:57,519
And the core?

64
00:07:57,687 --> 00:07:59,855
Dragon. Ahem.

65
00:08:00,022 --> 00:08:01,690
Dragon heartstring, my Lord.

66
00:08:01,858 --> 00:08:04,025
- Dragon heartstring.
- Mm.

67
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:21,543
To those of you who do not know...

68
00:08:21,711 --> 00:08:24,379
...we are joined tonight
by Miss Charity Burbage...

69
00:08:24,547 --> 00:08:30,051
...who, until recently, taught at Hogwarts
School of Witchcraft and Wizardry.

70
00:08:30,219 --> 00:08:33,680
Her specialty was Muggle Studies.

71
00:08:36,893 --> 00:08:43,148
It is Miss Burbage's belief
that Muggles are not so different from us.

72
00:08:43,316 --> 00:08:46,943
She would, given her way...

73
00:08:47,737 --> 00:08:49,654
...have us mate with them.

74
00:08:53,326 --> 00:08:59,539
To her, the mixture of magical
and Muggle blood is not an abomination...

75
00:08:59,707 --> 00:09:02,751
...but something to be encouraged.

76
00:09:03,794 --> 00:09:05,670
Severus.

77
00:09:05,838 --> 00:09:07,797
Severus, please.

78
00:09:09,467 --> 00:09:11,635
We're friends.

79
00:09:16,432 --> 00:09:17,974
Avada Kedavra!

80
00:09:28,236 --> 00:09:30,278
Nagini.

81
00:09:33,866 --> 00:09:35,533
Dinner.

82
00:11:20,848 --> 00:11:24,225
- Hello, Harry.
- All right. Wow.

83
00:11:24,393 --> 00:11:25,518
Hello.

84
00:11:25,686 --> 00:11:28,563
- You're looking fit.
- Yeah, he's absolutely gorgeous.

85
00:11:28,731 --> 00:11:31,232
What say we get undercover
before someone murders him?

86
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,400
Evening.

87
00:11:37,281 --> 00:11:38,907
I thought you were looking after...

88
00:11:39,075 --> 00:11:40,909
...the Prime Minister.
- You are more important.

89
00:11:41,952 --> 00:11:45,038
- Hello, Harry. Bill Weasley.
- Oh. Pleasure to meet you.

90
00:11:45,206 --> 00:11:48,208
- He was never always this handsome.
- Dead ugly.

91
00:11:48,375 --> 00:11:49,751
True enough.

92
00:11:49,919 --> 00:11:52,462
Owe it all to a werewolf,
name of Greyback.

93
00:11:52,630 --> 00:11:56,007
- Hope to repay the favor one day.
- You're still beautiful to me, William.

94
00:11:56,383 --> 00:12:00,011
Just remember, Fleur,
Bill takes his steaks on the raw side now.

95
00:12:00,179 --> 00:12:02,514
My husband, the joker.

96
00:12:02,681 --> 00:12:05,934
By the way, wait till you hear the news.
Remus and I...

97
00:12:06,102 --> 00:12:08,561
All right. We'll have time
for a cozy catch-up later.

98
00:12:08,729 --> 00:12:11,689
We've got to get the hell out of here.
And soon.

99
00:12:12,358 --> 00:12:15,610
Potter, you're underage, which means
you've still got the Trace on you.

100
00:12:15,778 --> 00:12:16,820
What's the Trace?

101
00:12:16,987 --> 00:12:19,656
If you sneeze, the Ministry will know
who wipes your nose.

102
00:12:19,824 --> 00:12:22,992
We have to use those means of transport
the Trace can't detect:

103
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:25,495
Brooms, Thestrals and the like.
We go in pairs.

104
00:12:25,663 --> 00:12:29,457
That way, if anyone's out there waiting
for us, and I reckon there will be...

105
00:12:29,625 --> 00:12:32,127
...they won't know which Harry Potter
is the real one.

106
00:12:32,545 --> 00:12:33,711
The real one?

107
00:12:35,047 --> 00:12:38,133
I believe you're familiar
with this particular brew.

108
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:40,635
No. Absolutely not.

109
00:12:40,803 --> 00:12:42,137
I told you he'd take it well.

110
00:12:42,304 --> 00:12:45,431
No, if you think I'm gonna let everyone
risk their lives for me, I...

111
00:12:45,599 --> 00:12:48,643
- Never done that before, have we?
- No. No. This is different.

112
00:12:48,811 --> 00:12:50,812
I mean, taking that, becoming me. No.

113
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:52,814
Well, none of us really fancy it, mate.

114
00:12:52,982 --> 00:12:57,152
Imagine if something went wrong, and
we ended up a scrawny, specky git forever.

115
00:12:57,319 --> 00:12:58,987
Everyone here is of age, Potter.

116
00:12:59,697 --> 00:13:01,156
They've all agreed to take the risk.

117
00:13:02,491 --> 00:13:05,410
Technically, I've been coerced.

118
00:13:05,578 --> 00:13:07,787
Mundungus Fletcher, Mr. Potter.

119
00:13:07,955 --> 00:13:10,498
- Always been a huge admirer.
- Nip it, Mundungus.

120
00:13:11,834 --> 00:13:14,335
All right, Granger, as discussed.

121
00:13:14,503 --> 00:13:17,213
- Blimey, Hermione.
- Straight in here, if you please.

122
00:13:27,099 --> 00:13:31,269
For those of you who haven't taken
Polyjuice Potion before, fair warning:

123
00:13:31,437 --> 00:13:33,062
It tastes like goblin piss.

124
00:13:33,230 --> 00:13:36,191
Have a lot of experiences with that,
do you, Mad-Eye?

125
00:13:37,109 --> 00:13:40,028
Just trying to diffuse the tension.

126
00:13:41,071 --> 00:13:42,864
Oh.

127
00:13:45,951 --> 00:13:47,702
Ugh.

128
00:14:11,977 --> 00:14:14,062
Wow, we're identical.

129
00:14:14,230 --> 00:14:15,230
Not yet, you're not.

130
00:14:18,943 --> 00:14:21,527
Haven't got anything
a bit more sporting, have you?

131
00:14:21,695 --> 00:14:23,154
I don't really fancy this color.

132
00:14:23,322 --> 00:14:26,115
- Well, fancy this, you're not you.
- So shut it and strip.

133
00:14:26,283 --> 00:14:27,867
All right, all right.

134
00:14:28,035 --> 00:14:29,577
You'll need to change too, Potter.

135
00:14:30,079 --> 00:14:32,747
Bill, look away. I'm hideous.

136
00:14:32,915 --> 00:14:35,208
I knew she was lying about that tattoo.

137
00:14:35,376 --> 00:14:37,794
Harry, your eyesight really is awful.

138
00:14:37,962 --> 00:14:41,673
Right, then. We'll be pairing off.
Each Potter will have a protector.

139
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:45,134
Mundungus, stick tight to me.
I wanna keep an eye on you.

140
00:14:45,678 --> 00:14:47,512
- As for Harry...
Yes?

141
00:14:48,347 --> 00:14:49,764
The real Harry.

142
00:14:49,932 --> 00:14:52,267
- Where the devil are you, anyway?
- Here.

143
00:14:52,434 --> 00:14:54,435
You'll ride with Hagrid.

144
00:14:54,603 --> 00:14:59,607
I brought you here 16 years ago when
you were no bigger than a Bowtruckle.

145
00:14:59,775 --> 00:15:01,567
Seems only right that I should be...

146
00:15:01,819 --> 00:15:05,780
...the one to take you away now.
- Yes, it's all very touching. Let's go.

147
00:15:19,169 --> 00:15:23,006
- Head for the Burrows.
- We'll rendezvous there.

148
00:15:23,549 --> 00:15:25,633
On the count of three.

149
00:15:25,801 --> 00:15:27,510
Hold tight, Harry.

150
00:15:27,678 --> 00:15:29,470
One...

151
00:15:30,347 --> 00:15:32,140
...two...

152
00:15:38,564 --> 00:15:40,356
...three!

153
00:16:10,345 --> 00:16:13,514
- Which one?
- Where are you?

154
00:16:14,725 --> 00:16:16,476
He's on your right!

155
00:16:16,643 --> 00:16:18,269
He's over there!

156
00:16:18,437 --> 00:16:20,104
Down!

157
00:16:25,569 --> 00:16:27,236
Hagrid, we have to help the others!

158
00:16:27,654 --> 00:16:30,531
I can't do that, Harry. Mad-Eye's orders.

159
00:16:37,498 --> 00:16:39,290
Hang on.

160
00:16:43,087 --> 00:16:45,171
Stupefy!

161
00:16:58,894 --> 00:16:59,977
Hang on, Harry.

162
00:17:09,905 --> 00:17:11,739
Hagrid.

163
00:17:28,966 --> 00:17:31,259
No. No.

164
00:17:53,323 --> 00:17:55,324
Harry.

165
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:18,366
Harry. Hagrid.

166
00:19:19,743 --> 00:19:23,204
What happened? Where are the others?

167
00:19:23,372 --> 00:19:24,538
Is no one else back?

168
00:19:24,706 --> 00:19:28,292
They were on us right from
the start, Molly. We didn't stand a chance.

169
00:19:28,460 --> 00:19:31,629
Well, thank goodness
you two are all right.

170
00:19:31,797 --> 00:19:34,382
The Death Eaters were
waiting for us. It was an ambush.

171
00:19:34,549 --> 00:19:36,926
Ron and Tonks
should've already been back.

172
00:19:37,094 --> 00:19:38,302
Dad and Fred as well.

173
00:19:41,223 --> 00:19:42,890
Here!

174
00:19:43,558 --> 00:19:46,978
Quick. Into the house.

175
00:19:50,649 --> 00:19:52,733
Oh, my boy.

176
00:19:54,903 --> 00:19:57,405
Oh. Oh.

177
00:19:58,991 --> 00:20:00,283
- Lupin!
- What are you doing?

178
00:20:02,828 --> 00:20:05,746
What creature sat in the corner...

179
00:20:05,914 --> 00:20:09,250
...the first time Harry Potter
visited my office in Hogwarts?

180
00:20:09,418 --> 00:20:11,043
- Are you mad?
- What creature?!

181
00:20:11,211 --> 00:20:13,045
A Grindylow.

182
00:20:19,386 --> 00:20:21,053
We've been betrayed.

183
00:20:21,221 --> 00:20:23,597
Voldemort knew
you were being moved tonight.

184
00:20:23,765 --> 00:20:26,684
I had to make sure
you weren't an impostor.

185
00:20:33,817 --> 00:20:35,276
Wait.

186
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:42,783
The last words Albus Dumbledore spoke
to the pair of us?

187
00:20:44,619 --> 00:20:48,956
"Harry is the best hope we have.
Trust him."

188
00:20:53,503 --> 00:20:54,628
What gave you away?

189
00:20:54,796 --> 00:20:57,923
Hedwig, I think.
She was trying to protect me.

190
00:21:14,524 --> 00:21:15,691
Thanks.

191
00:21:15,859 --> 00:21:18,027
Deserves that. Brilliant, he was.

192
00:21:18,195 --> 00:21:21,322
- I wouldn't be standing here without him.
- Really?

193
00:21:22,324 --> 00:21:24,992
Always the tone of surprise.

194
00:21:33,168 --> 00:21:34,377
We the last back?

195
00:21:35,670 --> 00:21:36,712
Where's George?

196
00:21:58,026 --> 00:22:00,236
How you feeling, Georgie?

197
00:22:02,239 --> 00:22:03,781
Saint-like.

198
00:22:04,991 --> 00:22:06,200
Come again?

199
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:10,704
Saint-like. I'm holy.

200
00:22:11,206 --> 00:22:14,291
I'm holey, Fred. Get it?

201
00:22:16,086 --> 00:22:20,798
The whole wide world of ear-related humor
and you go for "I'm holey."

202
00:22:20,966 --> 00:22:22,133
That's pathetic.

203
00:22:22,717 --> 00:22:25,052
Reckon I'm still better-looking than you.

204
00:22:28,557 --> 00:22:30,766
Mad-Eye's dead.

205
00:22:41,153 --> 00:22:44,905
Mundungus took one look at Voldemort
and Disapparated.

206
00:23:07,804 --> 00:23:09,847
Head for the Burrows.

207
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:12,016
This is beyond anything I imagined.

208
00:23:12,184 --> 00:23:14,810
- Seven?
- Seven...? A Horcrux.

209
00:23:14,978 --> 00:23:16,437
They could be hidden anywhere.

210
00:23:16,605 --> 00:23:18,772
To rip the soul into seven pieces...

211
00:23:18,940 --> 00:23:21,942
- If you did destroy each Horcrux...
- One destroys Voldemort.

212
00:23:25,530 --> 00:23:27,156
Trust me.

213
00:23:28,116 --> 00:23:31,660
You lied to me. Lied to me, Ollivander.

214
00:24:03,610 --> 00:24:05,528
Going somewhere?

215
00:24:09,199 --> 00:24:13,327
Nobody else is going to die. Not for me.

216
00:24:13,495 --> 00:24:15,287
For you?

217
00:24:15,455 --> 00:24:17,665
You think Mad-Eye died for you?

218
00:24:17,832 --> 00:24:20,793
You think George took that curse
for you?

219
00:24:21,545 --> 00:24:25,506
You may be the Chosen One, mate,
but this is a whole lot bigger than that.

220
00:24:25,674 --> 00:24:28,175
It's always been bigger than that.

221
00:24:30,387 --> 00:24:32,888
- Come with me.
- What, and leave Hermione?

222
00:24:33,348 --> 00:24:37,601
You mad?
We wouldn't last two days without her.

223
00:24:39,020 --> 00:24:40,521
Don't tell her I said that.

224
00:24:42,107 --> 00:24:45,317
Besides, you've still got
the Trace on you.

225
00:24:45,485 --> 00:24:49,572
- We've still got the wedding...
- I don't care about a wedding.

226
00:24:49,739 --> 00:24:54,618
I'm sorry. No matter whose it is.
I have to start finding these Horcruxes.

227
00:24:54,786 --> 00:24:56,745
They're our only chance to beat him...

228
00:24:56,913 --> 00:24:59,873
...and the longer we stay here,
the stronger he gets.

229
00:25:01,334 --> 00:25:03,419
Tonight's not the night, mate.

230
00:25:03,712 --> 00:25:06,213
We'd only be doing him a favor.

231
00:25:33,950 --> 00:25:35,909
Do you think he knows?

232
00:25:36,620 --> 00:25:42,499
I mean, they're bits of his soul,
these Horcruxes. Bits of him.

233
00:25:43,251 --> 00:25:47,504
When Dumbledore destroyed the ring,
you destroyed Tom Riddle's diary...

234
00:25:49,007 --> 00:25:51,592
...he must have felt something.

235
00:25:52,385 --> 00:25:56,096
To kill the other Horcruxes,
we have to find them.

236
00:25:56,473 --> 00:25:58,432
Where are they?

237
00:25:58,975 --> 00:26:01,060
Where do we start?

238
00:26:04,481 --> 00:26:05,606
Ready when you are.

239
00:26:07,317 --> 00:26:11,612
- Please pay attention!
- It's your brother's wedding. Buck up.

240
00:26:37,055 --> 00:26:39,139
Zip me up, will you?

241
00:26:52,987 --> 00:26:54,905
It seems silly, doesn't it, a wedding?

242
00:26:55,407 --> 00:26:57,783
Given everything that's going on.

243
00:26:59,119 --> 00:27:01,120
Maybe that's the best reason to have it...

244
00:27:01,788 --> 00:27:04,331
...because of everything that's going on.

245
00:27:20,348 --> 00:27:22,516
Morning.

246
00:27:32,694 --> 00:27:34,862
Come on, keep up.

247
00:27:35,613 --> 00:27:37,197
All together now.

248
00:27:37,365 --> 00:27:42,828
One, two, three.

249
00:27:52,881 --> 00:27:55,340
How's it looking at your end, boys?

250
00:27:55,967 --> 00:27:57,885
Brilliant.

251
00:28:00,013 --> 00:28:04,850
Bloody hell.
What's the Minister of Magic doing here?

252
00:28:10,732 --> 00:28:12,608
To what do we owe the pleasure,
Minister?

253
00:28:12,775 --> 00:28:17,362
I think we both know the answer
to that question, Mr. Potter.

254
00:28:25,038 --> 00:28:26,914
And this is...?

255
00:28:34,964 --> 00:28:38,884
"Herein is set forth
the last will and testament..."

256
00:28:39,052 --> 00:28:43,639
...of Albus Percival Wulfric
Brian Dumbledore.

257
00:28:43,806 --> 00:28:47,267
First, to Ronald Bilius Weasley...

258
00:28:48,436 --> 00:28:51,772
...I leave my Deluminator...

259
00:28:51,940 --> 00:28:54,191
...a device of my own making...

260
00:28:54,359 --> 00:28:59,613
...in the hope that,
when things seem most dark...

261
00:29:01,241 --> 00:29:04,117
"...it will show him the light."

262
00:29:09,999 --> 00:29:13,126
- Dumbledore left this for me?
- Yeah.

263
00:29:14,045 --> 00:29:15,629
Brilliant.

264
00:29:16,673 --> 00:29:18,507
What is it?

265
00:29:30,645 --> 00:29:32,271
Wicked.

266
00:29:35,525 --> 00:29:37,526
"To Hermione Jean Granger..."

267
00:29:37,694 --> 00:29:42,864
...I leave my copy of
The Tales of Beedle the Bard...

268
00:29:43,032 --> 00:29:47,703
"...in the hope that she find it
entertaining and instructive."

269
00:29:48,496 --> 00:29:49,830
Mom used to read me those.

270
00:29:50,707 --> 00:29:52,249
"The Wizard and the Hopping Pot."

271
00:29:52,417 --> 00:29:55,335
"Babbitty Rabbitty
and the Cackling Stump."

272
00:29:57,130 --> 00:30:00,507
Come on, Babbitty Rabbitty.

273
00:30:00,967 --> 00:30:02,676
No?

274
00:30:03,011 --> 00:30:05,804
"To Harry James Potter..."

275
00:30:06,347 --> 00:30:10,058
...I leave the Snitch he caught
in his first Quidditch match at Hogwarts...

276
00:30:10,226 --> 00:30:15,272
...as a reminder
of the rewards of perseverance...

277
00:30:17,525 --> 00:30:19,693
"...and skill."

278
00:30:39,756 --> 00:30:42,841
- Is that it, then?
- Not quite.

279
00:30:43,009 --> 00:30:48,388
Dumbledore left you a second bequest:

280
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:51,642
The sword of Godric Gryffindor.

281
00:30:53,227 --> 00:30:57,856
Unfortunately, the sword of Gryffindor
was not Dumbledore's to give away.

282
00:30:58,232 --> 00:31:00,984
As an important historical artifact,
it belongs...

283
00:31:01,152 --> 00:31:02,235
To Harry.

284
00:31:03,071 --> 00:31:05,030
It belongs to Harry.

285
00:31:05,198 --> 00:31:07,908
It came to him when he needed it
in the Chamber of Secrets.

286
00:31:08,076 --> 00:31:10,952
The sword may present itself
to any worthy Gryffindor.

287
00:31:11,120 --> 00:31:13,455
That does not make it
that wizard's property.

288
00:31:14,916 --> 00:31:18,543
And, in any event, the current
whereabouts of the sword are unknown.

289
00:31:18,711 --> 00:31:21,296
- Excuse me?
- The sword is missing.

290
00:31:22,674 --> 00:31:26,218
I don't know what you're up to,
Mr. Potter...

291
00:31:26,386 --> 00:31:30,347
...but you can't fight this war
on your own.

292
00:31:30,515 --> 00:31:32,933
He's too strong.

293
00:32:34,120 --> 00:32:35,370
Hello, Harry.

294
00:32:36,289 --> 00:32:40,292
I've interrupted a deep thought, haven't I?
I can see it growing smaller in your eyes.

295
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:42,002
Of course not. How are you, Luna?

296
00:32:42,170 --> 00:32:44,796
Very well. Got bitten by a garden gnome
only moments ago.

297
00:32:44,964 --> 00:32:47,299
Gnome saliva is very beneficial.

298
00:32:47,467 --> 00:32:49,843
Xenophilius Lovegood.
We live just over the hill.

299
00:32:50,011 --> 00:32:51,178
Pleasure to meet you, sir.

300
00:32:51,345 --> 00:32:54,139
I trust you know, Mr. Potter,
that we at The Quibbler...

301
00:32:54,307 --> 00:32:56,641
...unlike those toadies
at The Daily Prophet...

302
00:32:56,809 --> 00:32:59,394
...fully supported Dumbledore
in his lifetime...

303
00:32:59,562 --> 00:33:03,231
...and, in his death,
support you just as fully.

304
00:33:03,524 --> 00:33:04,900
Thank you.

305
00:33:05,067 --> 00:33:07,903
Come, Daddy.
Harry doesn't want to talk to us right now.

306
00:33:08,070 --> 00:33:10,363
He's just too polite to say so.

307
00:33:10,531 --> 00:33:12,616
Harry Potter.

308
00:33:16,162 --> 00:33:18,288
Excuse me, sir? May I sit down?

309
00:33:18,456 --> 00:33:21,875
Mr. Potter. By all means. Here.

310
00:33:22,043 --> 00:33:23,710
Thanks.

311
00:33:26,380 --> 00:33:29,716
I found what you wrote
in The Daily Prophet really moving.

312
00:33:30,259 --> 00:33:33,053
You obviously knew Dumbledore well.

313
00:33:33,221 --> 00:33:36,181
Well, I certainly knew him the longest.

314
00:33:36,349 --> 00:33:39,059
That is, if you don't count his brother,
Aberforth...

315
00:33:39,227 --> 00:33:42,270
...and somehow, people never do
seem to count Aberforth.

316
00:33:42,605 --> 00:33:44,689
- I didn't even know he had a brother.
- Ah.

317
00:33:44,857 --> 00:33:48,401
Well, Dumbledore was always
very private, even as a boy.

318
00:33:48,569 --> 00:33:49,986
Don't despair, Elphias.

319
00:33:50,154 --> 00:33:54,574
I'm told he's been thoroughly
unriddled by Rita Skeeter...

320
00:33:54,742 --> 00:33:57,577
...in 800 pages, no less.

321
00:33:58,246 --> 00:34:02,624
Word has it that someone talked to her.

322
00:34:02,792 --> 00:34:05,585
Someone who knew
the Dumbledore family well.

323
00:34:06,003 --> 00:34:09,589
Both you and I know who that is,
Elphias.

324
00:34:09,757 --> 00:34:11,258
A monstrous betrayal.

325
00:34:13,135 --> 00:34:14,761
Who are we talking about?

326
00:34:16,222 --> 00:34:18,348
Bathilda Bagshot.

327
00:34:20,017 --> 00:34:21,101
- Who?
- My God, boy...

328
00:34:21,269 --> 00:34:26,022
...she's only the most celebrated
magical historian of the last century.

329
00:34:27,733 --> 00:34:31,945
She was as close
to the Dumbledores as anyone.

330
00:34:32,113 --> 00:34:37,158
Oh, I'm sure Rita Skeeter thought
it well worth a trip to Godric's Hollow...

331
00:34:37,326 --> 00:34:40,537
...to take a peek
into that old bird's rattled cage.

332
00:34:40,705 --> 00:34:42,539
Godric's Hollow?

333
00:34:42,957 --> 00:34:44,875
Bathilda Bagshot
lives at Godric's Hollow?

334
00:34:45,293 --> 00:34:47,377
Well, that's where
she first met Dumbledore.

335
00:34:47,545 --> 00:34:49,421
You don't mean to say
he lived there too?

336
00:34:49,589 --> 00:34:53,133
The family moved there after his
father killed those three Muggles.

337
00:34:53,301 --> 00:34:56,970
Oh, it was quite the scandal.

338
00:34:57,138 --> 00:35:01,975
Honestly, my boy,
are you sure you knew him at all?

339
00:35:28,419 --> 00:35:31,504
The Ministry has fallen.

340
00:35:32,173 --> 00:35:36,051
The Minister of Magic is dead.

341
00:35:38,512 --> 00:35:40,847
They are coming.

342
00:35:41,015 --> 00:35:45,852
They are coming.

343
00:35:46,020 --> 00:35:47,520
They're coming!

344
00:35:49,523 --> 00:35:51,358
Nice meeting you, Mr. Potter.

345
00:36:02,453 --> 00:36:04,829
- Ginny!
- Harry! Go!

346
00:36:04,997 --> 00:36:06,039
Go!

347
00:36:19,387 --> 00:36:21,971
Here you go, sightseeing tour?
Leaves in 15 minutes.

348
00:36:23,391 --> 00:36:26,059
- Where are we?
- Shaftesbury Avenue.

349
00:36:26,227 --> 00:36:29,396
I used to come to the theater here
with Mom and Dad.

350
00:36:29,563 --> 00:36:31,815
I don't know why I thought of it.
It just popped into my head.

351
00:36:33,234 --> 00:36:35,068
This way.

352
00:36:38,864 --> 00:36:40,949
We need to change.

353
00:36:46,914 --> 00:36:48,164
How the ruddy...?

354
00:36:48,332 --> 00:36:50,917
Undetectable Extension Charm.

355
00:36:51,335 --> 00:36:53,586
You're amazing, you are.

356
00:36:53,796 --> 00:36:56,381
Always the tone of surprise.

357
00:36:58,384 --> 00:37:00,510
Ah. That'll be the books.

358
00:37:06,016 --> 00:37:07,892
What about all the people
at the wedding?

359
00:37:08,060 --> 00:37:10,520
- Do you think we should go back?
- They were after you.

360
00:37:10,688 --> 00:37:12,856
We'd put everyone in danger
by going back.

361
00:37:14,734 --> 00:37:16,443
- Ron's right.
- Ahem.

362
00:37:16,610 --> 00:37:18,278
Coffee?

363
00:37:18,821 --> 00:37:21,865
- A cappuccino, please.
- You?

364
00:37:22,700 --> 00:37:25,994
- What she said.
- Same.

365
00:37:29,373 --> 00:37:33,209
So where do we go from here?
Leaky Cauldron?

366
00:37:33,586 --> 00:37:34,669
It's too dangerous.

367
00:37:35,588 --> 00:37:39,132
If Voldemort has taken over the Ministry,
none of the old places are safe.

368
00:37:39,300 --> 00:37:42,343
Everyone from the wedding
will have gone underground, into hiding.

369
00:37:42,511 --> 00:37:45,013
My rucksack with all my things,
I've left it at the Burrow.

370
00:37:50,144 --> 00:37:52,061
You're joking.

371
00:37:53,647 --> 00:37:57,650
I've had all the essentials packed
for days, just in case.

372
00:37:57,818 --> 00:37:59,986
By the way, these jeans, not my favorite.

373
00:38:01,155 --> 00:38:02,238
Down!

374
00:38:03,365 --> 00:38:04,657
Stupefy!

375
00:38:08,871 --> 00:38:10,622
Expulso!

376
00:38:20,508 --> 00:38:22,342
Petrificus Totalus.

377
00:38:26,514 --> 00:38:27,555
Go.

378
00:38:28,015 --> 00:38:29,182
Leave.

379
00:38:33,854 --> 00:38:36,648
Lock the door, get the lights.

380
00:38:45,866 --> 00:38:47,617
This one's name is Rowle.

381
00:38:48,118 --> 00:38:51,538
He was on the Astronomy Tower
the night Snape killed Dumbledore.

382
00:38:52,373 --> 00:38:56,876
This is Dolohov. I recognize him
from the wanted posters.

383
00:38:57,920 --> 00:39:00,088
So, what we gonna do with you, hey?

384
00:39:00,965 --> 00:39:03,049
Kill us if it was turned round,
wouldn't you?

385
00:39:03,217 --> 00:39:04,551
If we kill them, they'll know we were here.

386
00:39:04,718 --> 00:39:06,135
Ron.

387
00:39:06,303 --> 00:39:10,265
Suppose he did Mad-Eye.
How would you feel then?

388
00:39:12,226 --> 00:39:13,893
It's better we wipe their memories.

389
00:39:14,728 --> 00:39:16,729
You're the boss.

390
00:39:17,022 --> 00:39:18,773
Hermione...

391
00:39:21,235 --> 00:39:23,736
...you're the best at spells.

392
00:39:41,380 --> 00:39:43,590
Obliviate.

393
00:39:55,936 --> 00:39:57,520
How is it they knew we were there?

394
00:39:57,688 --> 00:39:59,272
Maybe you still have the Trace on you?

395
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:02,901
Can't be. Trace breaks at 17.
It's wizarding law.

396
00:40:04,695 --> 00:40:06,279
What?

397
00:40:07,072 --> 00:40:10,033
We didn't celebrate your birthday, Harry.

398
00:40:10,409 --> 00:40:13,661
Ginny and I, we prepared a cake.

399
00:40:13,829 --> 00:40:16,789
We were going to bring it out
at the end of the wedding.

400
00:40:16,957 --> 00:40:20,418
I appreciate the thought, but given the
fact that we were almost killed...

401
00:40:20,586 --> 00:40:22,962
...by a couple of Death Eaters
a few minutes ago...

402
00:40:24,632 --> 00:40:26,341
Right.

403
00:40:27,134 --> 00:40:28,176
Perspective.

404
00:40:28,344 --> 00:40:31,346
We need to get off the streets,
get somewhere safe.

405
00:41:04,463 --> 00:41:06,506
What was that all about?

406
00:41:07,466 --> 00:41:13,304
Probably Mad-Eye's idea,
in case Snape decided to come snooping.

407
00:41:21,480 --> 00:41:23,439
Homenum Revelio.

408
00:41:30,072 --> 00:41:31,906
We're alone.

409
00:41:38,706 --> 00:41:40,957
I believed another wand...

410
00:41:41,125 --> 00:41:43,584
- You lied to me.
- It makes no sense.

411
00:41:46,422 --> 00:41:49,382
I believed a different wand would work,
I swear.

412
00:41:50,884 --> 00:41:52,969
There must be another way.

413
00:43:03,290 --> 00:43:07,043
Harry? Hermione, where are you?

414
00:43:07,294 --> 00:43:09,629
I think I've found something.

415
00:43:15,928 --> 00:43:16,969
Lovely.

416
00:43:22,684 --> 00:43:26,187
"Regulus Arcturus Black."

417
00:43:26,355 --> 00:43:28,064
R.A.B.

418
00:43:31,652 --> 00:43:34,987
"I know I will be dead
long before you read this."

419
00:43:35,155 --> 00:43:39,158
"I have stolen the real Horcrux
and intend to destroy it."

420
00:43:39,535 --> 00:43:41,953
R.A.B. is Sirius's brother.

421
00:43:42,371 --> 00:43:44,163
Yes.

422
00:43:46,250 --> 00:43:50,127
Question is,
did he actually destroy the real Horcrux?

423
00:44:11,859 --> 00:44:14,026
You've been spying on us, have you?

424
00:44:14,194 --> 00:44:18,656
Kreacher has been watching.

425
00:44:18,824 --> 00:44:20,741
Maybe he knows where the real locket is.

426
00:44:23,745 --> 00:44:25,705
Have you ever seen this before?

427
00:44:25,873 --> 00:44:27,456
Kreacher?

428
00:44:28,292 --> 00:44:30,710
It's Master Regulus' locket.

429
00:44:30,878 --> 00:44:33,588
But there were two, weren't there?

430
00:44:34,590 --> 00:44:36,299
Where's the other one?

431
00:44:38,802 --> 00:44:43,389
Kreacher doesn't know
where the other locket is.

432
00:44:43,557 --> 00:44:45,933
Yes, but did you ever see it?
Was it in this house?

433
00:44:46,101 --> 00:44:47,268
Filthy Mudblood.

434
00:44:47,436 --> 00:44:49,145
- Death Eaters are coming...
- Ron.

435
00:44:49,313 --> 00:44:52,148
- Blood traitor, Weasley.
- Answer her.

436
00:44:53,901 --> 00:44:56,152
Yes.

437
00:44:57,195 --> 00:45:00,656
It was here in this house.

438
00:45:01,909 --> 00:45:04,243
A most evil object.

439
00:45:04,411 --> 00:45:05,661
How do you mean?

440
00:45:06,413 --> 00:45:10,750
Before Master Regulus died,
he ordered Kreacher to destroy it...

441
00:45:10,918 --> 00:45:16,172
...but no matter how hard Kreacher tried,
he could not do it.

442
00:45:16,340 --> 00:45:17,924
Well, where is it now?

443
00:45:18,592 --> 00:45:23,179
- Did someone take it?
- He came in the night.

444
00:45:23,347 --> 00:45:28,017
He took many things,
including the locket.

445
00:45:28,185 --> 00:45:29,727
Who did?

446
00:45:30,395 --> 00:45:31,979
Who was it, Kreacher?

447
00:45:34,524 --> 00:45:37,193
Mundungus.

448
00:45:37,361 --> 00:45:40,863
Mundungus Fletcher.

449
00:45:41,949 --> 00:45:43,532
Find him.

450
00:46:05,055 --> 00:46:06,514
My father will hear about this.

451
00:46:11,812 --> 00:46:13,688
Hey, losers.

452
00:46:14,439 --> 00:46:16,649
He isn't here.

453
00:46:30,330 --> 00:46:32,707
As your new Minister for Magic...

454
00:46:32,916 --> 00:46:38,087
...I promise to restore
this temple of tolerance...

455
00:46:38,255 --> 00:46:39,922
...to its former glory.

456
00:46:41,341 --> 00:46:43,175
Therefore, beginning today...

457
00:46:44,219 --> 00:46:48,014
...each employee
will submit themselves...

458
00:46:48,682 --> 00:46:50,891
...for evaluation.

459
00:46:51,768 --> 00:46:54,770
You have nothing to fear...

460
00:46:56,189 --> 00:46:57,940
...if you have nothing to hide.

461
00:47:02,362 --> 00:47:03,946
- How much?
- Two Galleons.

462
00:47:04,114 --> 00:47:06,615
Come on, time is money. Cheers, pal.

463
00:47:06,783 --> 00:47:08,701
- Snatchers!
- Move out of the way.

464
00:47:14,916 --> 00:47:16,375
- I told you.
- Get out.

465
00:47:16,543 --> 00:47:17,585
Squash him.

466
00:47:26,803 --> 00:47:28,429
Be a bit gentler.

467
00:47:54,539 --> 00:47:56,665
They have flesh memories.

468
00:47:58,794 --> 00:48:04,340
When Scrimgeour first gave it to you,
I thought it might open at your touch.

469
00:48:05,175 --> 00:48:07,927
That Dumbledore had hidden
something inside it.

470
00:48:08,178 --> 00:48:09,845
Many of you are wondering...

471
00:48:10,013 --> 00:48:12,932
...why Voldemort has yet to show himself
now that he has vanquished...

472
00:48:13,100 --> 00:48:16,185
...the most powerful symbol of opposition
to him and his followers.

473
00:48:18,230 --> 00:48:19,271
Get off.

474
00:48:19,439 --> 00:48:22,191
Harry Potter, so long it's been.

475
00:48:22,651 --> 00:48:23,984
Get off me.

476
00:48:29,616 --> 00:48:33,536
As requested,
Kreacher has returned with the thief...

477
00:48:33,703 --> 00:48:35,704
- Expelliarmus.
- ...Mundungus Fletcher.

478
00:48:35,872 --> 00:48:39,083
What you playing at? Setting a pair
of bleeding house-elves after me.

479
00:48:39,251 --> 00:48:40,751
Dobby was only trying to help.

480
00:48:40,919 --> 00:48:45,297
Dobby saw Kreacher in Diagon Alley,
which Dobby thought was curious.

481
00:48:45,465 --> 00:48:49,802
And then Dobby heard Kreacher
mention Harry Potter's name.

482
00:48:49,970 --> 00:48:52,805
- I just...
- And then Dobby saw Kreacher...

483
00:48:52,973 --> 00:48:55,766
...talking with the thief, Mundungus...
- I'm no thief.

484
00:48:55,934 --> 00:48:58,853
You foul little... Git.

485
00:48:59,271 --> 00:49:03,649
I'm a purveyor
of rare and wondrous objects.

486
00:49:03,817 --> 00:49:05,693
You're a thief, Dung. Everyone knows it.

487
00:49:05,861 --> 00:49:08,821
Master Weasley,
so good to see you again.

488
00:49:08,989 --> 00:49:10,030
Wicked trainers.

489
00:49:11,783 --> 00:49:14,535
Listen, I panicked that night, all right?

490
00:49:16,163 --> 00:49:18,414
Could I help it
if Mad-Eye fell off his broom?

491
00:49:20,417 --> 00:49:21,834
- You...
- Tell the truth.

492
00:49:22,002 --> 00:49:24,795
When you turned this place over...
Don't deny it.

493
00:49:24,963 --> 00:49:26,505
...You found a locket, am I right?

494
00:49:26,673 --> 00:49:28,924
Why? Was it valuable?

495
00:49:29,092 --> 00:49:30,217
You still got it?

496
00:49:30,385 --> 00:49:32,845
No, he's worried
he didn't get enough money for it.

497
00:49:33,013 --> 00:49:34,513
Bleeding give it away, didn't I?

498
00:49:35,891 --> 00:49:39,018
There I was,
flogging me wares in Diagon Alley...

499
00:49:39,186 --> 00:49:43,189
...when some Ministry hag comes up
and asks to see me license.

500
00:49:43,398 --> 00:49:45,482
Says she's a mind to lock me up.

501
00:49:45,650 --> 00:49:49,320
And would've done it too,
if she hadn't taken a fancy to that locket.

502
00:49:49,487 --> 00:49:53,407
- Who was she? The witch. Do you know?
- No, I...

503
00:49:58,205 --> 00:50:01,624
Well, she's there. Look.

504
00:50:03,752 --> 00:50:06,128
Bleeding bow and all.

505
00:50:46,962 --> 00:50:50,756
Right, remember what we said.

506
00:50:51,007 --> 00:50:54,760
Don't speak to anyone
unless absolutely necessary.

507
00:50:55,011 --> 00:50:59,932
Just try and act normal.
Do what everybody else is doing.

508
00:51:00,350 --> 00:51:03,477
If we do that, then with a bit of luck,
we'll get inside.

509
00:51:03,645 --> 00:51:05,270
- And then...
- it gets really tricky.

510
00:51:05,438 --> 00:51:07,272
- Correct.
- Yeah.

511
00:51:07,440 --> 00:51:10,359
- This is completely mental.
- Completely.

512
00:51:10,527 --> 00:51:12,569
The world's mental.

513
00:51:12,737 --> 00:51:14,154
Come on...

514
00:51:14,781 --> 00:51:17,199
...we've got a Horcrux to find.

515
00:52:11,087 --> 00:52:13,505
We flush ourselves in.

516
00:52:17,510 --> 00:52:20,304
That's bloody disgusting.

517
00:52:48,333 --> 00:52:50,000
Name?

518
00:52:51,294 --> 00:52:52,836
You. Come.

519
00:52:53,004 --> 00:52:55,172
- What? What?
- Come on.

520
00:52:55,340 --> 00:52:57,758
- What did I do?
- Just keep walking.

521
00:53:05,141 --> 00:53:07,059
- Are those...?
- Muggles.

522
00:53:07,227 --> 00:53:11,855
In their rightful place.

523
00:53:13,608 --> 00:53:16,819
Gotta tell you,
I'm starting to freak out a bit.

524
00:53:19,072 --> 00:53:23,575
How long did you say this batch
of Polyjuice would last, Hermione?

525
00:53:24,119 --> 00:53:25,160
I didn't.

526
00:53:32,335 --> 00:53:34,253
Cattermole.

527
00:53:35,296 --> 00:53:38,924
It's still raining inside my office.
That's two days now.

528
00:53:40,844 --> 00:53:42,594
Have you tried an umbrella?

529
00:53:43,596 --> 00:53:46,515
You do realize I'm going downstairs,
don't you, Cattermole?

530
00:53:47,100 --> 00:53:51,061
- Downstairs?
- To interrogate your wife.

531
00:53:51,938 --> 00:53:55,899
Now, if my wife's blood status
were in doubt...

532
00:53:56,067 --> 00:53:58,944
...and the head of the Department
of Magical Law Enforcement...

533
00:53:59,112 --> 00:54:04,700
...needed a job doing,
I think I might just make that a priority.

534
00:54:05,285 --> 00:54:07,452
You have one hour.

535
00:54:19,215 --> 00:54:24,887
Oh, my God. What am I gonna do?
My wife's all alone downstairs.

536
00:54:25,180 --> 00:54:29,474
- Ron, you don't have a wife.
- Oh, right.

537
00:54:29,642 --> 00:54:31,602
Level 2.

538
00:54:32,395 --> 00:54:34,521
But how do I stop it raining?

539
00:54:34,689 --> 00:54:37,316
Try "Finite Incantatem."

540
00:54:37,483 --> 00:54:39,318
Department of Magical Law Enforcement...

541
00:54:39,485 --> 00:54:40,944
...and Improper Use of Magic Department.

542
00:54:41,112 --> 00:54:43,071
This is you, Ron.

543
00:54:47,327 --> 00:54:52,164
Finite Incantatem. Okay.
And if that doesn't work...?

544
00:55:04,052 --> 00:55:07,012
Level 1,
Minister of Magic and support staff.

545
00:55:07,180 --> 00:55:09,306
If we don't locate Umbridge
within the hour...

546
00:55:09,474 --> 00:55:11,475
...we go find Ron
and come back another day.

547
00:55:11,643 --> 00:55:12,684
- Deal?
- Yes.

548
00:55:16,231 --> 00:55:18,565
Ah, Mafalda. Travers sent you, did he?

549
00:55:18,733 --> 00:55:21,818
Good, we'll go straight down.

550
00:55:24,155 --> 00:55:26,698
Albert, aren't you getting out?

551
00:56:00,066 --> 00:56:02,067
Runcorn.

552
00:56:54,579 --> 00:56:55,954
Accio locket.

553
00:57:50,676 --> 00:57:53,845
- All right, all right.
- Let's calm down, shall we?

554
00:57:54,722 --> 00:57:57,182
Let's get back to work, please.

555
00:57:58,017 --> 00:57:59,851
Calm down.

556
00:58:05,191 --> 00:58:06,858
Runcorn.

557
00:58:14,700 --> 00:58:16,451
Morning.

558
00:58:18,162 --> 00:58:20,580
Ron, it's me.

559
00:58:20,748 --> 00:58:24,584
Harry.
Blimey, forgot what you looked like.

560
00:58:24,752 --> 00:58:26,211
Where's Hermione?

561
00:58:26,379 --> 00:58:29,798
She's gone down to the courtrooms,
with Umbridge.

562
00:58:36,639 --> 00:58:38,765
Bloody cold down here.

563
00:58:38,933 --> 00:58:42,561
I'm a half-blood. My father was a wizard.

564
00:58:42,728 --> 00:58:44,980
William Alderton.
He worked here for 30 years.

565
00:58:45,231 --> 00:58:48,650
Perhaps you know him.
Always wore his jacket inside out.

566
00:58:48,818 --> 00:58:51,278
No, there's been a mistake.
I'm half-blood, you see.

567
00:58:51,445 --> 00:58:54,656
We must go back. I'm half-blood.

568
00:59:04,750 --> 00:59:06,877
- Mary Elizabeth Cattermole?
- Yes.

569
00:59:07,044 --> 00:59:11,965
Of 27 Chislehurst Gardens,
Great Tolling, Evesham?

570
00:59:12,133 --> 00:59:13,175
- Yes.
- It's here.

571
00:59:13,342 --> 00:59:18,138
Mother to Maisie, Ellie and Alfred?
Wife to Reginald?

572
00:59:22,351 --> 00:59:23,435
Reg?

573
00:59:34,989 --> 00:59:36,823
Thank you, Albert.

574
00:59:39,452 --> 00:59:42,162
Mary Elizabeth Cattermole?

575
00:59:44,373 --> 00:59:45,457
Yes.

576
00:59:46,459 --> 00:59:50,003
A wand was taken from you
upon your arrival at the Ministry today.

577
00:59:50,171 --> 00:59:52,964
Is this that wand?

578
00:59:54,800 --> 00:59:59,304
Would you please tell the court from which
witch or wizard you took this wand?

579
00:59:59,472 --> 01:00:01,932
I didn't take it.

580
01:00:03,142 --> 01:00:08,980
I got it in Diagon Alley, at Ollivander's,
when I was 11.

581
01:00:10,399 --> 01:00:12,901
It chose me.

582
01:00:14,278 --> 01:00:16,029
You're lying.

583
01:00:16,489 --> 01:00:21,034
Wands only choose witches,
and you are not a witch.

584
01:00:21,202 --> 01:00:23,245
But I am.

585
01:00:23,663 --> 01:00:26,748
Tell them, Reg. Tell them what I am.

586
01:00:29,293 --> 01:00:30,669
Reg, tell them what I am.

587
01:00:40,638 --> 01:00:42,389
What on earth are you doing, Albert?

588
01:00:45,309 --> 01:00:47,185
You're lying, Dolores.

589
01:00:49,563 --> 01:00:52,148
And one mustn't tell lies.

590
01:00:52,942 --> 01:00:54,234
Stupefy!

591
01:01:01,951 --> 01:01:03,326
It's Harry Potter.

592
01:01:03,494 --> 01:01:05,954
It is, isn't it?
This'll be one to tell the kids.

593
01:01:21,971 --> 01:01:23,138
Expecto Patronum!

594
01:01:46,996 --> 01:01:49,414
Oh. Oh. Oh.

595
01:01:49,582 --> 01:01:51,624
Mary, go home.

596
01:01:53,085 --> 01:01:54,544
Get the kids.

597
01:01:54,712 --> 01:01:58,089
I'll meet you there. We have to get out
of the country, understand?

598
01:01:58,257 --> 01:02:00,717
Mary, do as I say.

599
01:02:15,107 --> 01:02:16,274
Mary?

600
01:02:17,943 --> 01:02:19,819
Who's that?

601
01:02:20,946 --> 01:02:23,948
Long story. Nice meeting you.

602
01:02:24,116 --> 01:02:25,492
It's Harry Potter.

603
01:02:26,202 --> 01:02:28,161
It's Harry. Harry Potter.

604
01:02:28,329 --> 01:02:30,372
- There he is.
- Get him!

605
01:02:30,539 --> 01:02:32,624
- Get him!
- Stop him!

606
01:02:44,553 --> 01:02:45,720
- Watch out.
- Look out.

607
01:02:46,097 --> 01:02:47,472
This way!

608
01:03:06,492 --> 01:03:08,326
Expelliarmus!

609
01:03:55,749 --> 01:03:56,833
Oh, my God.

610
01:03:57,001 --> 01:04:00,628
Shh, shh, shh. It's all right. It's okay.

611
01:04:03,090 --> 01:04:06,301
Harry. Harry, quickly, in my bag.

612
01:04:06,469 --> 01:04:09,012
There's a bottle labeled
"Essence of Dittany."

613
01:04:11,557 --> 01:04:14,392
Shh. Shh.

614
01:04:14,560 --> 01:04:17,228
Okay, okay. Quickly.

615
01:04:18,022 --> 01:04:20,106
- Accio Dittany.
- Shh.

616
01:04:20,483 --> 01:04:23,234
It's all right. Unstopper it.

617
01:04:23,402 --> 01:04:24,819
Hermione, his arm.

618
01:04:25,070 --> 01:04:27,071
I know, just do it.

619
01:04:27,781 --> 01:04:29,532
It's okay.

620
01:04:30,784 --> 01:04:34,746
- Okay, it's gonna sting a little bit.
- What happened? I thought we meant...

621
01:04:34,914 --> 01:04:37,665
...to be going back to Grimmauld Place.
- We were. We were. Shh.

622
01:04:37,833 --> 01:04:39,667
It's all right. One more, one more.

623
01:04:39,835 --> 01:04:44,380
We were there, we were there,
but Yaxley had hold of me, and I...

624
01:04:44,548 --> 01:04:47,592
I knew once he'd seen where we were,
we couldn't stay...

625
01:04:47,760 --> 01:04:50,887
...so I brought us here...

626
01:04:51,347 --> 01:04:53,973
...but Ron got splinched.

627
01:04:57,061 --> 01:04:58,853
It's all right.

628
01:05:17,915 --> 01:05:20,291
Protege Totalum.

629
01:05:21,752 --> 01:05:23,211
Salvio Hexia.

630
01:05:23,379 --> 01:05:24,796
What are you doing?

631
01:05:24,964 --> 01:05:27,257
Protective enchantments.

632
01:05:27,424 --> 01:05:31,010
I don't fancy another visit like the one
we had in Shaftesbury Avenue, do you?

633
01:05:31,178 --> 01:05:32,887
You can get going on the tent.

634
01:05:33,555 --> 01:05:35,390
- Tent?
- Protege Totalum.

635
01:05:35,557 --> 01:05:37,684
Where am I supposed to find a tent?

636
01:05:37,851 --> 01:05:42,146
Repello Muggletum. Muffliato.

637
01:05:52,491 --> 01:05:53,783
You first.

638
01:05:57,371 --> 01:05:59,497
Dissendium.

639
01:06:13,095 --> 01:06:15,013
Incendio.

640
01:06:20,394 --> 01:06:22,437
Expulso.

641
01:06:29,653 --> 01:06:31,779
Diffindo.

642
01:06:33,198 --> 01:06:34,240
Reducto.

643
01:06:55,679 --> 01:06:57,555
What are you doing?

644
01:06:58,932 --> 01:07:01,726
We have to keep it safe
until we find out how to destroy it.

645
01:07:01,894 --> 01:07:04,562
Seems strange, mate.
Dumbledore sends you off...

646
01:07:04,730 --> 01:07:08,524
...to find all these Horcruxes,
but doesn't tell you how to destroy them.

647
01:07:08,692 --> 01:07:10,318
Doesn't that bother you?

648
01:07:22,706 --> 01:07:26,084
A goblin by the name of Gornuk was killed.

649
01:07:26,251 --> 01:07:29,337
It is believed that Muggle-born
Dean Thomas and a second goblin...

650
01:07:29,505 --> 01:07:32,423
...both believed to have been traveling
with Tonks, Cresswell...

651
01:07:32,591 --> 01:07:34,133
...and Gornuk, may have escaped.

652
01:07:34,301 --> 01:07:38,096
If Dean is listening or anyone has
any knowledge of his whereabouts...

653
01:07:38,263 --> 01:07:41,307
...his parents and sisters
are desperate for news.

654
01:07:41,475 --> 01:07:44,852
Meanwhile, a Muggle family of five
has been found dead in their home.

655
01:07:45,020 --> 01:07:48,272
You know the spell, Harry.

656
01:07:52,027 --> 01:07:53,277
Tell me.

657
01:07:55,948 --> 01:07:57,782
Tell me, Gregorovitch.

658
01:07:57,950 --> 01:07:59,575
It was stolen from me.

659
01:07:59,743 --> 01:08:03,204
Who was he? The thief?

660
01:08:06,333 --> 01:08:10,294
It was a boy. It was he who took it.

661
01:08:10,671 --> 01:08:12,964
I never saw it again.

662
01:08:13,132 --> 01:08:14,966
I swear on my life.

663
01:08:15,801 --> 01:08:16,968
I believe you.

664
01:08:22,975 --> 01:08:24,725
Avada Kedavra!

665
01:08:39,366 --> 01:08:40,867
I thought it had stopped.

666
01:08:42,786 --> 01:08:45,204
You can't keep letting him in, Harry.

667
01:08:47,291 --> 01:08:50,209
You-Know-Who has found Gregorovitch.

668
01:08:50,502 --> 01:08:52,086
The wandmaker?

669
01:08:52,254 --> 01:08:56,799
He wants something
that Gregorovitch used to have...

670
01:08:56,967 --> 01:08:58,426
...but I don't know what.

671
01:08:58,594 --> 01:09:04,599
But he wants it desperately.
I mean, it's as if his life depends on it.

672
01:09:06,143 --> 01:09:07,685
Don't.

673
01:09:07,853 --> 01:09:10,021
- It comforts him.
- It sets my teeth on edge.

674
01:09:10,189 --> 01:09:12,440
What's he expecting to hear,
good news?

675
01:09:12,608 --> 01:09:15,485
- -Who long expected it,
the fall of the Ministry was shocking.

676
01:09:15,652 --> 01:09:18,029
I think he just hopes
he doesn't hear bad news.

677
01:09:18,197 --> 01:09:20,114
We promise
to remain your eyes and ears...

678
01:09:20,282 --> 01:09:21,699
How long before he can travel?

679
01:09:21,867 --> 01:09:25,077
- -Bringing you news when we can,
from wherever we can.

680
01:09:25,245 --> 01:09:26,537
I'm doing everything I can.

681
01:09:26,705 --> 01:09:28,247
You're not doing enough!

682
01:09:31,001 --> 01:09:33,044
Take it off.

683
01:09:33,795 --> 01:09:36,380
I said, take it off now.

684
01:09:47,392 --> 01:09:50,102
- Better?
- Loads.

685
01:09:53,815 --> 01:09:56,067
We'll take it in turns, okay?

686
01:10:25,138 --> 01:10:28,516
Finch does admit
his invention currently has one short.

687
01:10:28,684 --> 01:10:30,142
And now, other news:

688
01:10:30,310 --> 01:10:33,604
Severus Snape, newly appointed
headmaster of Hogwarts...

689
01:10:33,772 --> 01:10:37,525
...has decreed that all students
must conform to the latest house rules.

690
01:11:05,137 --> 01:11:07,638
Hogwarts bears little resemblance
to the school...

691
01:11:07,931 --> 01:11:09,599
...under Dumbledore's leadership.

692
01:11:09,766 --> 01:11:13,394
Snape's curriculum is severe,
reflecting the wishes of the Dark Lord...

693
01:11:14,229 --> 01:11:19,150
...and infractions are dealt with harshly
by the two Death Eaters on staff.

694
01:11:38,670 --> 01:11:40,004
What's that?

695
01:11:49,264 --> 01:11:52,016
What's that smell?

696
01:12:14,498 --> 01:12:16,540
- What you doing?
- It's heavy.

697
01:12:16,708 --> 01:12:18,292
Oh, sorry. Do you want me to carry it?

698
01:12:18,460 --> 01:12:21,379
- Yeah, thank you.
- Don't be ridiculous. Pick it up.

699
01:12:22,964 --> 01:12:24,006
Numpty.

700
01:12:29,096 --> 01:12:31,097
Snatchers.

701
01:12:32,140 --> 01:12:34,558
Good to know your enchantments work.

702
01:12:39,606 --> 01:12:43,234
He could smell it. My perfume.

703
01:12:45,445 --> 01:12:47,530
I've told you...

704
01:12:47,989 --> 01:12:49,824
...Ron isn't strong enough to Apparate.

705
01:12:49,991 --> 01:12:53,744
Well, then, we'll go on foot.

706
01:12:54,538 --> 01:12:59,458
And next time, Hermione, as much as
I like your perfume, just don't wear any.

707
01:13:04,381 --> 01:13:08,259
And now for the names
of missing witches and wizards.

708
01:13:09,094 --> 01:13:11,262
These are confirmed.

709
01:13:12,097 --> 01:13:15,474
Thankfully, the list is short today.

710
01:13:16,226 --> 01:13:18,269
Jason and Alison Denbright.

711
01:13:19,146 --> 01:13:20,187
Oh. Thank you.

712
01:13:20,355 --> 01:13:24,108
Bella, Jake, Charlie and Madge Farley.

713
01:13:24,443 --> 01:13:25,443
Joe Laurie.

714
01:13:26,778 --> 01:13:29,363
Eleanor Sarah Gibbs.

715
01:13:30,532 --> 01:13:33,826
Harry and Bronwyn Trigg.

716
01:13:35,454 --> 01:13:38,497
Rob and Ellie Dowson.

717
01:13:39,624 --> 01:13:42,126
Georgia Clark-Day.

718
01:13:42,711 --> 01:13:45,254
Joshua Flexson.

719
01:13:45,630 --> 01:13:47,131
George Coutas.

720
01:13:48,300 --> 01:13:51,135
Gabriella and Emily Mather.

721
01:13:52,137 --> 01:13:55,264
Jacob and Mimi Erland.

722
01:13:56,308 --> 01:13:57,808
William and Brian Gallagher.

723
01:13:57,976 --> 01:14:00,436
He doesn't know
what he's doing, does he?

724
01:14:03,273 --> 01:14:05,149
None of us do.

725
01:14:07,736 --> 01:14:10,488
Toby and Olivia Gleaves.

726
01:14:11,364 --> 01:14:13,991
Katie and James Killick.

727
01:14:14,159 --> 01:14:16,660
Elsie Valentine Schroeder.

728
01:14:17,746 --> 01:14:19,830
Jennifer Winston.

729
01:14:19,998 --> 01:14:23,125
Tamsin and Iola Hillicker.

730
01:14:24,336 --> 01:14:25,336
Scarlet and Kitty Sharp.

731
01:14:44,356 --> 01:14:46,190
Oh, my God.

732
01:14:46,525 --> 01:14:48,192
What?

733
01:14:48,735 --> 01:14:50,778
I'll tell you in a minute.

734
01:14:51,321 --> 01:14:54,031
Maybe you could tell me now.

735
01:14:54,366 --> 01:14:57,409
The sword of Gryffindor,
it's goblin-made.

736
01:14:57,577 --> 01:14:58,702
Brilliant.

737
01:14:59,746 --> 01:15:02,164
No, you don't understand.

738
01:15:02,499 --> 01:15:04,875
Dirt and rust have no effect
on the blade.

739
01:15:05,877 --> 01:15:09,213
It only takes in
that which makes it stronger.

740
01:15:09,631 --> 01:15:11,006
Okay.

741
01:15:11,800 --> 01:15:14,677
Harry, you've already destroyed
one Horcrux, right?

742
01:15:14,844 --> 01:15:17,096
Tom Riddle's diary
in the Chamber of Secrets.

743
01:15:17,264 --> 01:15:20,182
With a Basilisk fang.
If you tell me you've got one of those...

744
01:15:20,350 --> 01:15:23,811
...in that bloody beaded bag of yours...
- Don't you see?

745
01:15:23,979 --> 01:15:27,731
In the Chamber of Secrets, you stabbed
the Basilisk with the sword of Gryffindor.

746
01:15:27,899 --> 01:15:31,402
Its blade is impregnated
with Basilisk venom.

747
01:15:31,570 --> 01:15:33,696
It only takes in
that which makes it stronger.

748
01:15:33,863 --> 01:15:37,032
- Exactly, which is why...
- it can destroy Horcruxes.

749
01:15:37,200 --> 01:15:39,451
That's why Dumbledore left it to you
in his will.

750
01:15:39,619 --> 01:15:44,039
You are brilliant, Hermione. Truly.

751
01:15:44,207 --> 01:15:48,252
Actually, I'm highly logical, which
allows me to look past extraneous detail...

752
01:15:48,420 --> 01:15:50,921
...and perceive clearly
that which others overlook.

753
01:15:51,089 --> 01:15:53,799
Yeah, there's only one problem,
of course.

754
01:15:59,180 --> 01:16:01,307
The sword was stolen.

755
01:16:02,726 --> 01:16:05,269
Yeah, I'm still here.

756
01:16:05,770 --> 01:16:09,898
But you two carry on.
Don't let me spoil the fun.

757
01:16:11,276 --> 01:16:15,279
- What's wrong?
- Wrong? Nothing's wrong.

758
01:16:15,447 --> 01:16:17,323
Not according to you, anyway.

759
01:16:17,490 --> 01:16:21,118
Look, if you've got something to say,
don't be shy. Spit it out.

760
01:16:21,494 --> 01:16:24,788
All right, I'll spit it out.
But don't expect me to be grateful...

761
01:16:24,956 --> 01:16:27,499
...because there's another damn thing
we've gotta find.

762
01:16:27,667 --> 01:16:29,960
I thought you knew
what you signed up for.

763
01:16:30,462 --> 01:16:32,296
Yeah. I thought I did too.

764
01:16:32,464 --> 01:16:35,507
Well, then I'm sorry,
but I don't quite understand.

765
01:16:35,675 --> 01:16:39,136
What part of this isn't living up
to your expectations?

766
01:16:39,304 --> 01:16:41,597
Did you think we were gonna
be staying in a hotel?

767
01:16:41,765 --> 01:16:45,017
Finding a Horcrux every other day?
Thought you'd be back by Christmas?

768
01:16:45,185 --> 01:16:47,019
I just thought, after all this time...

769
01:16:47,187 --> 01:16:50,648
...we would've achieved something.
I thought you knew what you were doing.

770
01:16:50,815 --> 01:16:53,192
I thought Dumbledore told you
something worthwhile.

771
01:16:53,360 --> 01:16:56,570
- I thought you had a plan.
- I told you everything Dumbledore told me.

772
01:16:56,738 --> 01:16:58,947
In case you haven't noticed,
we found a Horcrux.

773
01:16:59,115 --> 01:17:02,993
Yeah, and we're as close to getting rid of
it as we are to finding the rest of them.

774
01:17:03,161 --> 01:17:05,746
Ron. Please, take...

775
01:17:06,289 --> 01:17:08,666
Take the Horcrux off.
You wouldn't be saying this...

776
01:17:08,833 --> 01:17:10,167
...if you hadn't been wearing it all day.

777
01:17:10,335 --> 01:17:12,753
Want to know why I listen to that radio?

778
01:17:13,838 --> 01:17:17,591
To make sure I don't hear Ginny's name,
or Fred, or George or Mom.

779
01:17:17,759 --> 01:17:20,844
You think I'm not listening?
You think I don't know how this feels?!

780
01:17:21,137 --> 01:17:22,554
No, you don't know how it feels!

781
01:17:22,722 --> 01:17:25,099
Your parents are dead.
You have no family.

782
01:17:26,184 --> 01:17:28,936
- Stop. Stop.
- Fine, then go!

783
01:17:29,771 --> 01:17:30,938
Go, then!

784
01:17:33,858 --> 01:17:34,858
Fine.

785
01:17:38,029 --> 01:17:39,697
Ron.

786
01:17:42,909 --> 01:17:44,702
And you?

787
01:17:46,454 --> 01:17:48,997
Are you coming or you staying?

788
01:17:56,089 --> 01:17:59,174
Fine. I get it.

789
01:17:59,801 --> 01:18:01,760
I saw you two the other night.

790
01:18:02,178 --> 01:18:04,596
Ron, that's... That's nothing.

791
01:18:06,725 --> 01:18:08,100
Ron...

792
01:18:11,312 --> 01:18:13,647
Ron, where are you going?

793
01:18:14,649 --> 01:18:16,900
Please, come back.

794
01:18:18,361 --> 01:18:20,070
Ron.

795
01:18:24,743 --> 01:18:25,784
Ron!

796
01:19:28,097 --> 01:19:30,724
Salvio Hexia.

797
01:19:34,187 --> 01:19:36,647
Repellum Muggletum.

798
01:19:39,692 --> 01:19:42,152
Salvio Hexia.

799
01:20:03,466 --> 01:20:06,134
Poor old Jim's white as a ghost

800
01:20:06,928 --> 01:20:10,138
He's found the answer that we lost

801
01:20:10,515 --> 01:20:13,976
We're all weeping now
Weeping because

802
01:20:14,519 --> 01:20:20,107
There ain't nothing we can do
To protect you

803
01:20:20,483 --> 01:20:23,986
O children

804
01:20:27,907 --> 01:20:30,507
Lift up your voice

805
01:20:37,500 --> 01:20:39,710
Children

806
01:20:43,423 --> 01:20:49,177
Rejoice, rejoice

807
01:20:49,345 --> 01:20:52,723
Hey, little train, we're jumping on

808
01:20:52,890 --> 01:20:56,643
The train that goes to the kingdom

809
01:20:57,186 --> 01:21:00,355
We're happy, Ma
We're having fun

810
01:21:00,523 --> 01:21:04,651
And the train ain't even left the station

811
01:21:04,819 --> 01:21:08,196
Hey, little train, wait for me

812
01:21:08,406 --> 01:21:12,242
I once was blind but now I see

813
01:21:12,410 --> 01:21:15,746
Have you left a seat for me?

814
01:21:15,913 --> 01:21:20,042
Is that such a stretch of the imagination?

815
01:21:20,209 --> 01:21:23,545
Hey, little train, wait for me

816
01:21:23,713 --> 01:21:27,591
I was held in chains but now I'm free

817
01:21:27,884 --> 01:21:30,761
I'm hanging in there
Don't you see?

818
01:21:30,928 --> 01:21:35,432
In this process of elimination

819
01:21:35,600 --> 01:21:38,727
Hey, little train, we're jumping on

820
01:21:38,936 --> 01:21:42,439
The train that goes to the kingdom

821
01:21:43,024 --> 01:21:46,318
We're happy, Ma
We're having fun

822
01:21:46,486 --> 01:21:50,405
It's beyond my wildest expectation

823
01:21:50,573 --> 01:21:53,784
Hey, little train, we're jumping on

824
01:21:53,951 --> 01:21:57,621
The train that goes to the kingdom

825
01:21:58,122 --> 01:22:01,333
We're happy, Ma
We're having fun

826
01:22:01,501 --> 01:22:06,380
The train ain't even left the station

827
01:22:53,094 --> 01:22:54,594
Hermione.

828
01:22:54,846 --> 01:22:57,097
Hermione? You were right.

829
01:22:57,265 --> 01:22:58,849
Snitches have flesh memories...

830
01:22:59,016 --> 01:23:03,645
...but I didn't catch the first Snitch
with my hand, I almost swallowed it.

831
01:23:08,901 --> 01:23:11,695
- "I open at the close."
- What do you think that means?

832
01:23:11,863 --> 01:23:13,238
I don't know.

833
01:23:15,658 --> 01:23:18,034
I found something as well.

834
01:23:24,417 --> 01:23:27,878
At first I thought it was an eye,
but now I don't think it is.

835
01:23:28,045 --> 01:23:32,215
It isn't a rune, and it isn't anywhere
in Spellman's Syllabary.

836
01:23:32,717 --> 01:23:35,802
Somebody inked it in. It isn't part
of the book. Somebody drew it.

837
01:23:35,970 --> 01:23:39,639
Luna's dad was wearing that
at Bill and Fleur's wedding.

838
01:23:42,393 --> 01:23:45,687
Why would someone draw it
in a children's book?

839
01:23:48,274 --> 01:23:50,734
Look, Hermione, I've been thinking.

840
01:23:51,277 --> 01:23:53,403
I want to go to Godric's Hollow.

841
01:23:53,571 --> 01:23:56,615
It's where I was born.
It's where my parents died.

842
01:23:56,783 --> 01:24:00,410
That's exactly where he'll expect you to go
because it means something to you.

843
01:24:00,578 --> 01:24:02,996
Yeah, but it means something to him too,
Hermione.

844
01:24:03,164 --> 01:24:05,165
You-Know-Who almost died there.

845
01:24:05,333 --> 01:24:10,003
I mean, isn't that exactly the type of
place he'd be likely to hide a Horcrux?

846
01:24:10,963 --> 01:24:13,548
It's dangerous, Harry.

847
01:24:15,134 --> 01:24:19,137
But even I have to admit, recently
I've been thinking we'll have to go there.

848
01:24:19,305 --> 01:24:21,765
I think it's possible
something else is hidden there.

849
01:24:21,933 --> 01:24:23,433
What?

850
01:24:24,143 --> 01:24:25,852
The sword.

851
01:24:26,437 --> 01:24:30,232
If Dumbledore wanted you to find it, but
didn't want it in the Ministry's hands...

852
01:24:30,399 --> 01:24:34,611
...where better to hide it than the
birthplace of the founder of Gryffindor?

853
01:24:35,947 --> 01:24:37,781
Hermione...

854
01:24:43,037 --> 01:24:45,789
Don't ever let me
give you a haircut again.

855
01:25:07,019 --> 01:25:09,688
I still think we should've used
Polyjuice Potion.

856
01:25:09,856 --> 01:25:11,398
No.

857
01:25:12,066 --> 01:25:14,276
This is where I was born.

858
01:25:14,610 --> 01:25:16,987
I'm not returning as someone else.

859
01:25:26,831 --> 01:25:29,833
Good night. Ha-ha-ha.

860
01:25:32,837 --> 01:25:35,630
Harry, I think it's Christmas Eve.

861
01:25:37,133 --> 01:25:38,425
Listen.

862
01:25:44,140 --> 01:25:46,975
Do you think they'd be in there,
Hermione?

863
01:25:47,393 --> 01:25:49,394
My mom and dad.

864
01:25:55,359 --> 01:25:57,611
Yeah, I think they would.

865
01:26:34,190 --> 01:26:37,233
"Ignotus Peverell."

866
01:26:39,320 --> 01:26:40,946
Hey, Harry?

867
01:27:18,818 --> 01:27:21,027
Merry Christmas, Hermione.

868
01:27:22,321 --> 01:27:24,572
Merry Christmas, Harry.

869
01:27:44,427 --> 01:27:49,806
Harry, there's someone
watching us. By the church.

870
01:28:00,526 --> 01:28:02,360
I think I know who that is.

871
01:28:04,238 --> 01:28:05,655
I don't like this, Harry.

872
01:28:05,823 --> 01:28:10,869
Hermione, she knew
Dumbledore. She might have the sword.

873
01:28:29,722 --> 01:28:31,347
This is where they died, Hermione.

874
01:28:38,939 --> 01:28:41,399
This is where he murdered them.

875
01:28:53,913 --> 01:28:55,872
You're Bathilda, aren't you?

876
01:29:01,462 --> 01:29:03,546
Here, let me do that.

877
01:29:27,696 --> 01:29:31,574
Miss Bagshot, who is this man?

878
01:29:43,212 --> 01:29:44,879
Harry.

879
01:29:48,926 --> 01:29:50,760
Lumos.

880
01:31:31,153 --> 01:31:32,195
Harry!

881
01:32:22,997 --> 01:32:24,080
Confringo!

882
01:33:06,790 --> 01:33:08,958
Are you feeling better?

883
01:33:12,004 --> 01:33:14,464
You've outdone yourself this time,
Hermione.

884
01:33:14,631 --> 01:33:16,758
The Forest of Dean.

885
01:33:17,718 --> 01:33:22,096
I came here once with Mom and Dad,
years ago.

886
01:33:22,723 --> 01:33:24,849
It's just how I remember it.

887
01:33:25,267 --> 01:33:29,187
The trees, the river, everything.

888
01:33:29,480 --> 01:33:32,315
Like nothing's changed.

889
01:33:33,567 --> 01:33:36,569
Not true, of course.
Everything's changed.

890
01:33:37,529 --> 01:33:41,324
If I brought my parents back here now,
they probably wouldn't recognize any of it.

891
01:33:43,452 --> 01:33:47,580
Not the trees, not the river...

892
01:33:49,333 --> 01:33:51,501
...not even me.

893
01:33:56,632 --> 01:33:59,425
Maybe we should just stay here, Harry.

894
01:34:01,428 --> 01:34:03,554
Grow old.

895
01:34:09,561 --> 01:34:12,855
You wanted to know
who the boy in the photograph was.

896
01:34:13,607 --> 01:34:14,690
I know.

897
01:34:15,859 --> 01:34:18,277
Gellert Grindelwald.

898
01:34:25,202 --> 01:34:28,621
He's the thief I saw
in Gregorovitch's Wand Shop.

899
01:34:28,789 --> 01:34:32,041
Speaking of which, where is my wand?

900
01:34:33,377 --> 01:34:35,795
Where's my wand, Hermione?

901
01:34:44,429 --> 01:34:48,933
As we were leaving Godric's Hollow,
I cast a curse and it rebounded.

902
01:34:51,687 --> 01:34:52,895
I'm sorry.

903
01:34:53,564 --> 01:34:56,232
- I tried to mend it, but wands are different.
- It's done.

904
01:34:58,193 --> 01:35:02,155
Leave me yours.
Go inside and get warm.

905
01:35:02,573 --> 01:35:04,907
I'll take the locket as well.

906
01:35:17,421 --> 01:35:18,796
Trust me.

907
01:36:44,549 --> 01:36:46,175
Lumos.

908
01:37:27,259 --> 01:37:28,634
Accio sword.

909
01:37:34,474 --> 01:37:36,392
Diffindo.

910
01:39:16,827 --> 01:39:19,995
- Hermione?
- Are you mental?

911
01:39:21,164 --> 01:39:22,748
It was you?

912
01:39:22,916 --> 01:39:26,669
Well, yeah. Bit obvious, I think.

913
01:39:26,837 --> 01:39:28,671
And you cast the doe as well, did you?

914
01:39:29,214 --> 01:39:32,883
- No, I thought that was you.
- No, my Patronus is a stag.

915
01:39:33,051 --> 01:39:35,261
Right. Yeah. Antlers.

916
01:39:38,431 --> 01:39:41,600
Okay, Ron. Do it.

917
01:39:42,561 --> 01:39:46,313
I can't handle it. That thing affects me
more than it affects you and Hermione.

918
01:39:46,857 --> 01:39:49,483
- All the more reason.
- No. I can't.

919
01:39:49,651 --> 01:39:50,860
Then why are you here?

920
01:39:52,279 --> 01:39:54,363
Why did you come back?

921
01:40:01,913 --> 01:40:06,041
Now, I'll have to speak to it in order for
it to open. When it does, don't hesitate.

922
01:40:06,668 --> 01:40:09,211
I don't know what's in there,
but it'll put up a fight.

923
01:40:09,379 --> 01:40:12,047
The bit of Riddle that was in that diary
tried to kill me.

924
01:40:14,551 --> 01:40:17,636
All right. One...

925
01:40:19,222 --> 01:40:20,306
...two...

926
01:40:20,974 --> 01:40:22,892
...three.

927
01:40:33,111 --> 01:40:38,240
I have seen your heart, and it is mine.

928
01:40:40,827 --> 01:40:44,747
I have seen your dreams,
Ronald Weasley...

929
01:40:44,915 --> 01:40:47,291
...and I have seen your fears.

930
01:40:49,002 --> 01:40:53,172
Least loved by your mother,
who craved a daughter.

931
01:40:53,798 --> 01:40:58,802
Least loved by the girl
who prefers your friend.

932
01:40:58,970 --> 01:41:01,722
Ron, kill it!

933
01:41:08,146 --> 01:41:10,856
We were better without you.

934
01:41:11,358 --> 01:41:13,108
Happier without you.

935
01:41:13,276 --> 01:41:18,614
Who could look at you
compared to Harry Potter?

936
01:41:19,866 --> 01:41:23,202
What are you
compared with the Chosen One?

937
01:41:23,370 --> 01:41:24,536
Ron, it's lying!

938
01:41:24,704 --> 01:41:27,706
Your mother confessed
she would have preferred me as a son.

939
01:41:27,874 --> 01:41:30,876
What woman would take you?

940
01:41:31,086 --> 01:41:34,255
You are nothing.

941
01:41:34,422 --> 01:41:35,547
Nothing.

942
01:41:36,299 --> 01:41:40,344
Nothing compared to him.

943
01:42:30,895 --> 01:42:32,563
Just think...

944
01:42:33,481 --> 01:42:35,566
...only three to go.

945
01:42:38,611 --> 01:42:40,362
Hermione?

946
01:42:42,615 --> 01:42:44,366
Hermione?

947
01:42:48,872 --> 01:42:50,831
Is everything all right?

948
01:42:51,458 --> 01:42:56,128
It's fine.
Actually, you know, it's more than fine.

949
01:43:00,550 --> 01:43:02,176
Hey.

950
01:43:06,389 --> 01:43:12,603
You complete ass, Ronald Weasley!

951
01:43:12,771 --> 01:43:16,440
You show up here after weeks,
and you say "hey"?

952
01:43:18,651 --> 01:43:21,403
- Where's my wand? Where's my wand?
- I don't know.

953
01:43:21,571 --> 01:43:23,822
- Harry Potter, give me my wand.
- I don't have it.

954
01:43:23,990 --> 01:43:27,826
- How come he's got your wand?
- Never mind why he's got my wand.

955
01:43:30,080 --> 01:43:31,330
What is that?

956
01:43:34,250 --> 01:43:35,292
You destroyed it.

957
01:43:38,588 --> 01:43:42,591
And how is it that you just happen
to have the sword of Gryffindor?

958
01:43:42,967 --> 01:43:44,927
It's a long story.

959
01:43:48,098 --> 01:43:52,226
- Don't think this changes anything.
- Oh, of course not.

960
01:43:52,394 --> 01:43:55,646
I only just destroyed a bloody Horcrux.
Why would that change anything?

961
01:43:55,814 --> 01:43:59,900
Look, I wanted to come back
as soon as I left.

962
01:44:00,068 --> 01:44:03,487
- I just didn't know how to find you.
- Yeah, how did you find us?

963
01:44:03,655 --> 01:44:06,740
With this. It doesn't just turn off lights.

964
01:44:06,908 --> 01:44:11,787
I don't know how it works, but Christmas
morning I was sleeping in this little pub...

965
01:44:11,955 --> 01:44:14,415
...keeping away from some Snatchers...

966
01:44:14,833 --> 01:44:16,125
...and I heard it.

967
01:44:16,501 --> 01:44:17,960
It?

968
01:44:19,295 --> 01:44:21,213
A voice...

969
01:44:22,799 --> 01:44:24,007
...your voice, Hermione...

970
01:44:25,176 --> 01:44:26,802
...coming out of it.

971
01:44:26,970 --> 01:44:30,806
- And what exactly did I say, may I ask?
- My name.

972
01:44:31,433 --> 01:44:33,475
Just my name.

973
01:44:34,227 --> 01:44:36,311
Like a whisper.

974
01:44:38,314 --> 01:44:44,319
So I took it, clicked it,
and this tiny ball of light appeared.

975
01:44:44,779 --> 01:44:46,196
And I knew.

976
01:44:46,781 --> 01:44:51,410
And sure enough, it floated toward me,
the ball of light...

977
01:44:53,121 --> 01:44:57,332
...went right to my chest,
straight through me. Right here.

978
01:44:58,501 --> 01:45:02,504
And I knew it was gonna take me
where I needed to go, so I Disapparated...

979
01:45:02,672 --> 01:45:04,965
...and came to this hillside.

980
01:45:05,508 --> 01:45:08,010
It was dark. I had no idea where I was.

981
01:45:08,553 --> 01:45:11,388
I just hoped
that one of you would show yourself.

982
01:45:12,307 --> 01:45:13,849
And you did.

983
01:45:31,242 --> 01:45:34,161
I've always liked these flames
Hermione makes.

984
01:45:38,208 --> 01:45:40,751
How long do you reckon
she'll stay mad at me?

985
01:45:42,295 --> 01:45:45,631
Well, just keep talking about that
little ball of light touching your heart...

986
01:45:45,798 --> 01:45:47,216
...and she'll come round.

987
01:45:47,383 --> 01:45:50,135
It was true. Every word.

988
01:45:51,930 --> 01:45:54,306
This is gonna sound crazy...

989
01:45:54,766 --> 01:45:59,144
...but I think that's why Dumbledore
left it to me, the Deluminator.

990
01:45:59,646 --> 01:46:04,650
I think he knew that somehow I'd need it
to find my way back, and she'd lead me.

991
01:46:07,529 --> 01:46:10,239
Bloody hell, I just realized,
you need a wand, don't you?

992
01:46:10,406 --> 01:46:12,908
- Yeah.
- I've got one here.

993
01:46:13,201 --> 01:46:15,786
It's a blackthorn. Ten inches.

994
01:46:15,954 --> 01:46:19,581
Nothing special, but I reckon it'll do.

995
01:46:19,999 --> 01:46:22,793
Took if off a Snatcher
a couple of weeks ago.

996
01:46:23,294 --> 01:46:27,130
Don't tell Hermione this,
but they're a bit dim, Snatchers.

997
01:46:27,423 --> 01:46:30,342
This one was definitely part troll,
the smell of him.

998
01:46:30,510 --> 01:46:31,552
Engorgio.

999
01:46:31,719 --> 01:46:33,887
- Reducio!
- What's going on in there?

1000
01:46:34,055 --> 01:46:35,305
- Nothing.
- Nothing.

1001
01:46:37,684 --> 01:46:39,309
We need to talk.

1002
01:46:40,103 --> 01:46:41,311
Yeah, all right.

1003
01:46:48,278 --> 01:46:51,822
- I want to go see Xenophilius Lovegood.
- Sorry?

1004
01:46:53,616 --> 01:46:55,242
See this?

1005
01:46:55,410 --> 01:46:59,288
It's a letter Dumbledore wrote
to Grindelwald. Look at the signature.

1006
01:47:00,498 --> 01:47:02,708
It's the mark again.

1007
01:47:03,626 --> 01:47:05,794
It keeps cropping up.

1008
01:47:05,962 --> 01:47:10,299
In Beedle the Bard,
in the graveyard in Godric's Hollow.

1009
01:47:11,134 --> 01:47:13,010
It was there too.

1010
01:47:13,177 --> 01:47:16,805
- Where?
- Outside Gregorovitch's Wand Shop.

1011
01:47:17,223 --> 01:47:18,473
But what does it mean?

1012
01:47:18,641 --> 01:47:23,437
Look, you've got no idea where
the next Horcrux is, and neither do I...

1013
01:47:25,148 --> 01:47:28,066
...but this, this means something.

1014
01:47:28,401 --> 01:47:31,820
- I'm sure of it.
- Yeah. Hermione's right.

1015
01:47:32,822 --> 01:47:34,948
We ought to see Lovegood.

1016
01:47:35,450 --> 01:47:39,161
Let's vote on it. Those in favor?

1017
01:48:03,019 --> 01:48:05,646
You're not still mad at him, are you?

1018
01:48:05,938 --> 01:48:08,190
I'm always mad at him.

1019
01:48:10,985 --> 01:48:12,486
Luna.

1020
01:48:12,654 --> 01:48:14,363
Luna.

1021
01:48:22,038 --> 01:48:24,873
"Keep off the dirigible plums."

1022
01:48:33,883 --> 01:48:36,593
What is it? Who are you?

1023
01:48:36,886 --> 01:48:37,928
What do you want?

1024
01:48:38,096 --> 01:48:42,724
Hello, Mr. Lovegood. I'm Harry Potter.
We met a few months ago.

1025
01:48:46,729 --> 01:48:48,605
Could we come in?

1026
01:48:52,402 --> 01:48:54,986
- Where is Luna?
- Luna?

1027
01:48:56,239 --> 01:48:58,240
She'll be along.

1028
01:49:11,754 --> 01:49:13,797
So how can I help you, Mr. Potter?

1029
01:49:14,632 --> 01:49:17,676
Well, actually...

1030
01:49:18,678 --> 01:49:23,223
It was about something you were wearing
round your neck at the wedding. A symbol.

1031
01:49:24,767 --> 01:49:26,643
You mean this?

1032
01:49:27,061 --> 01:49:28,645
Yes.

1033
01:49:28,938 --> 01:49:30,814
That exactly.

1034
01:49:31,482 --> 01:49:35,444
What we've wondered is, what is it?

1035
01:49:35,611 --> 01:49:37,446
What is it?

1036
01:49:37,613 --> 01:49:40,615
Well, it's the sign of the Deathly Hallows,
of course.

1037
01:49:40,783 --> 01:49:41,867
- The what?
- The what?

1038
01:49:42,034 --> 01:49:44,119
The Deathly Hallows.

1039
01:49:44,287 --> 01:49:47,372
I assume you're all familiar with
"The Tale of the Three Brothers."

1040
01:49:47,540 --> 01:49:48,957
- Yes.
- No.

1041
01:49:54,380 --> 01:49:56,131
I have it in here.

1042
01:50:07,393 --> 01:50:09,019
"There were once three brothers...

1043
01:50:09,187 --> 01:50:13,607
...who were traveling along a lonely,
winding road at twilight."

1044
01:50:13,774 --> 01:50:16,485
Midnight. Mom always said "midnight."

1045
01:50:21,491 --> 01:50:25,368
But "twilight's" fine. Better, actually.

1046
01:50:27,663 --> 01:50:29,498
Do you want to read it?

1047
01:50:29,665 --> 01:50:31,875
No. It's fine.

1048
01:50:33,794 --> 01:50:35,712
"There were once three brothers..."

1049
01:50:35,880 --> 01:50:41,092
...who were traveling along a lonely,
winding road at twilight.

1050
01:50:42,970 --> 01:50:48,266
In time, the brothers reached a river
too treacherous to pass.

1051
01:50:48,601 --> 01:50:50,477
But being learned in the magical arts...

1052
01:50:50,645 --> 01:50:55,815
...the three brothers simply
waved their wands and made a bridge.

1053
01:50:57,151 --> 01:50:59,236
Before they could cross, however...

1054
01:50:59,403 --> 01:51:03,532
...they found their path blocked
by a hooded figure.

1055
01:51:03,783 --> 01:51:07,661
It was Death, and he felt cheated.

1056
01:51:07,828 --> 01:51:10,872
Cheated because travelers would
normally drown in the river.

1057
01:51:11,040 --> 01:51:13,124
But Death was cunning.

1058
01:51:13,751 --> 01:51:16,753
He pretended to congratulate
the three brothers on their magic...

1059
01:51:16,921 --> 01:51:22,217
...and said that each had earned a prize for
having been clever enough to evade him.

1060
01:51:22,760 --> 01:51:27,347
The oldest asked for a wand
more powerful than any in existence.

1061
01:51:27,515 --> 01:51:32,102
So Death fashioned him one
from an elder tree that stood nearby.

1062
01:51:33,521 --> 01:51:37,816
The second brother decided he wanted
to humiliate Death even further...

1063
01:51:37,984 --> 01:51:42,404
...and asked for the power
to recall loved ones from the grave.

1064
01:51:42,863 --> 01:51:47,158
So Death plucked a stone from the river
and offered it to him.

1065
01:51:47,910 --> 01:51:51,871
Finally,
Death turned to the third brother.

1066
01:51:53,082 --> 01:51:54,499
A humble man...

1067
01:51:54,667 --> 01:51:58,878
...he asked for something that would
allow him to go forth from that place...

1068
01:51:59,046 --> 01:52:02,215
...without being followed by Death.

1069
01:52:03,301 --> 01:52:09,180
And so it was that Death reluctantly
handed over his own Cloak of invisibility.

1070
01:52:12,560 --> 01:52:15,478
The first brother traveled
to a distant village...

1071
01:52:15,646 --> 01:52:17,772
...where, with the Elder Wand in hand...

1072
01:52:17,940 --> 01:52:21,693
...he killed a wizard
with whom he had once quarreled.

1073
01:52:23,904 --> 01:52:27,449
Drunk with the power
that the Elder Wand had given him...

1074
01:52:27,617 --> 01:52:30,702
...he bragged of his invincibility.

1075
01:52:33,706 --> 01:52:37,167
But that night,
another wizard stole the wand...

1076
01:52:37,335 --> 01:52:40,462
...and slit the brother's throat
for good measure.

1077
01:52:40,671 --> 01:52:44,132
And so Death took the first brother
for his own.

1078
01:52:44,842 --> 01:52:46,801
The second brother journeyed
to his home...

1079
01:52:46,969 --> 01:52:49,971
...where he took the stone
and turned it thrice in hand.

1080
01:52:50,139 --> 01:52:54,601
To his delight, the girl he'd once hoped
to marry before her untimely death...

1081
01:52:54,769 --> 01:52:57,145
...appeared before him.

1082
01:52:57,647 --> 01:53:02,942
Yet, soon she turned sad and cold
for she did not belong in the mortal world.

1083
01:53:03,110 --> 01:53:04,736
Driven mad with hopeless longing...

1084
01:53:04,904 --> 01:53:08,198
...the second brother killed himself
so as to join her.

1085
01:53:09,408 --> 01:53:12,494
And so Death took the second brother.

1086
01:53:12,662 --> 01:53:14,329
As for the third brother...

1087
01:53:14,497 --> 01:53:18,708
...Death searched for many years
but was never able to find him.

1088
01:53:18,876 --> 01:53:21,795
Only when he attained a great age
did the youngest brother...

1089
01:53:21,962 --> 01:53:26,216
...shed the Cloak of invisibility
and give it to his son.

1090
01:53:27,468 --> 01:53:31,596
He then greeted Death as an old friend
and went with him gladly...

1091
01:53:31,764 --> 01:53:34,933
"...departing this life as equals."

1092
01:53:37,019 --> 01:53:41,523
- So there you are.
- Those are the Deathly Hallows.

1093
01:53:42,900 --> 01:53:45,985
I'm sorry, sir.
I still don't quite understand.

1094
01:53:51,575 --> 01:53:53,702
Where's that pen I had?

1095
01:54:04,672 --> 01:54:05,922
The Elder Wand.

1096
01:54:07,049 --> 01:54:10,719
The most powerful wand ever made.

1097
01:54:21,105 --> 01:54:23,398
The Resurrection Stone.

1098
01:54:34,285 --> 01:54:38,079
The Cloak of invisibility.

1099
01:54:40,082 --> 01:54:43,251
Together, they make the Deathly Hallows.

1100
01:54:43,502 --> 01:54:48,965
Together, they make one
master of Death.

1101
01:54:54,180 --> 01:54:57,849
That mark was on a grave
in Godric's Hollow.

1102
01:54:58,934 --> 01:55:01,603
Uh, Mr. Lovegood,
does the Peverell Family...

1103
01:55:01,771 --> 01:55:03,605
...have anything to do
with the Deathly Hallows?

1104
01:55:03,773 --> 01:55:06,608
Uh... Uh...

1105
01:55:06,776 --> 01:55:10,528
Ignotus... Excuse me... and his brothers,
Cadmus and Antioch...

1106
01:55:10,696 --> 01:55:13,364
...are thought to be the original owners
of the Hallows...

1107
01:55:13,532 --> 01:55:18,411
...and therefore the inspiration
for the story. Uh... Uh...

1108
01:55:18,579 --> 01:55:21,080
But your tea's gone cold.

1109
01:55:22,291 --> 01:55:24,292
I'll be right back.

1110
01:55:24,460 --> 01:55:26,294
Let's go down here.

1111
01:55:28,172 --> 01:55:29,672
Let's get out of here.

1112
01:55:29,840 --> 01:55:32,717
I'm not drinking any more of that stuff,
hot or cold.

1113
01:55:39,016 --> 01:55:40,975
Thank you, sir.

1114
01:55:41,894 --> 01:55:44,938
- You forgot the water.
- Water?

1115
01:55:45,105 --> 01:55:46,523
For the tea.

1116
01:55:46,690 --> 01:55:49,275
Did...? Did I?

1117
01:55:51,195 --> 01:55:53,363
How silly of me.

1118
01:55:54,990 --> 01:55:57,242
It's no matter.
We really should be going anyway.

1119
01:55:57,409 --> 01:55:59,494
No, you can't!

1120
01:56:03,666 --> 01:56:05,375
Sir?

1121
01:56:12,758 --> 01:56:15,343
You're my only hope.

1122
01:56:19,223 --> 01:56:23,601
They were angry, you see,
about what I'd been writing.

1123
01:56:26,647 --> 01:56:28,773
So they took her.

1124
01:56:30,234 --> 01:56:33,027
They took my Luna.

1125
01:56:34,697 --> 01:56:36,364
My Luna.

1126
01:56:48,836 --> 01:56:51,713
But it's really you they want.

1127
01:56:53,966 --> 01:56:56,050
Who took her, sir?

1128
01:57:01,181 --> 01:57:02,432
Voldemort.

1129
01:57:13,068 --> 01:57:15,403
Stop! I've got him!

1130
01:57:32,671 --> 01:57:36,591
That treacherous little bleeder.
Is there no one we can trust?

1131
01:57:36,759 --> 01:57:39,052
They kidnapped her
because he supported me.

1132
01:57:39,219 --> 01:57:41,346
He was just desperate.

1133
01:57:41,889 --> 01:57:44,098
I'll do the enchantments.

1134
01:57:55,778 --> 01:57:57,195
Hello, beautiful.

1135
01:58:02,660 --> 01:58:06,287
Well, don't hang about, snatch them.

1136
01:59:17,526 --> 01:59:19,026
Harry.

1137
01:59:19,194 --> 01:59:22,196
Tell me, Grindelwald.
Tell me where it is.

1138
01:59:22,781 --> 01:59:26,868
Grindelwald. Grindelwald. Grindelwald.

1139
01:59:27,578 --> 01:59:31,038
Hello, Tom.
I knew you would come one day...

1140
01:59:31,540 --> 01:59:35,501
...but surely you must know
I no longer have what you seek.

1141
01:59:36,128 --> 01:59:39,172
- Tell me, Grindelwald. Tell me where it is.
- Ha-ha-ha.

1142
01:59:39,339 --> 01:59:40,715
Tell me who possesses it.

1143
01:59:40,883 --> 01:59:46,012
The Elder Wand lies with him,
of course...

1144
01:59:46,180 --> 01:59:48,431
...buried in the earth.

1145
01:59:49,391 --> 01:59:50,725
Dumbledore.

1146
01:59:59,735 --> 02:00:01,611
The Hallows exist...

1147
02:00:01,779 --> 02:00:05,573
...but he's only after one of them,
the last one. He knows where it is.

1148
02:00:05,741 --> 02:00:09,577
He's gonna have it by the end of the night.
You-Know-Who's found the Elder Wand.

1149
02:00:09,745 --> 02:00:12,246
- Don't touch her. Unh!
- Leave him.

1150
02:00:12,414 --> 02:00:13,664
Your boyfriend will get worse than that...

1151
02:00:13,832 --> 02:00:14,957
Get off me.

1152
02:00:15,125 --> 02:00:17,877
...If he doesn't learn to behave himself.

1153
02:00:21,089 --> 02:00:22,590
What happened to you, ugly?

1154
02:00:24,301 --> 02:00:26,177
No, not you.

1155
02:00:27,596 --> 02:00:30,640
- What's your name?
- Dudley. Vernon Dudley.

1156
02:00:30,808 --> 02:00:33,017
Check it.

1157
02:00:34,603 --> 02:00:36,938
And you, my lovely...

1158
02:00:40,275 --> 02:00:42,276
...what do they call you?

1159
02:00:43,695 --> 02:00:47,782
Penelope Clearwater, half-blood.

1160
02:00:50,869 --> 02:00:52,787
There's no Vernon Dudley on here.

1161
02:00:53,872 --> 02:00:57,124
- Did you hear that, ugly?
- The list says you're lying.

1162
02:00:57,292 --> 02:00:59,502
How come you don't want us
to know who you are?

1163
02:00:59,670 --> 02:01:02,338
The list's wrong. I told you who I am.

1164
02:01:18,313 --> 02:01:20,398
Change of plan.

1165
02:01:21,483 --> 02:01:24,735
We're not taking this lot to the Ministry.

1166
02:02:04,401 --> 02:02:08,029
Get Draco.

1167
02:02:12,534 --> 02:02:14,076
Well?

1168
02:02:17,205 --> 02:02:21,709
- I can't be sure.
- Draco. Look closely, son.

1169
02:02:22,711 --> 02:02:27,798
If we are the ones
to hand Potter over to the Dark Lord...

1170
02:02:27,966 --> 02:02:33,220
...everything would be forgiven.
All would be as it was, you understand?

1171
02:02:33,388 --> 02:02:37,516
Now, we won't be forgetting who
actually caught him, I hope, Mr. Malfoy.

1172
02:02:37,684 --> 02:02:40,102
You dare to
talk to me like that in my own house?

1173
02:02:40,270 --> 02:02:42,063
Lucius.

1174
02:02:44,983 --> 02:02:48,819
Don't be shy, sweetie. Come over.

1175
02:02:50,322 --> 02:02:55,076
Now, if this isn't who we think it is,
Draco, and we call him, he'll kill us all.

1176
02:02:55,243 --> 02:02:58,079
We need to be absolutely sure.

1177
02:02:58,372 --> 02:02:59,372
What's wrong with his face?

1178
02:02:59,539 --> 02:03:01,248
Yes, what is wrong with his face?

1179
02:03:01,416 --> 02:03:03,084
He came to us like that.

1180
02:03:03,335 --> 02:03:04,752
Something he picked up in the forest,
I reckon.

1181
02:03:04,920 --> 02:03:08,631
Or ran into a Stinging Jinx.
Was it you, dearie?

1182
02:03:13,762 --> 02:03:16,514
Give me her wand.
We'll see what her last spell was.

1183
02:03:17,766 --> 02:03:19,266
Ah.

1184
02:03:19,559 --> 02:03:20,601
Got you.

1185
02:03:23,772 --> 02:03:25,481
What is that?

1186
02:03:27,442 --> 02:03:29,026
Where'd you get that from?

1187
02:03:29,194 --> 02:03:32,697
It was in her bag when we searched her.
Reckon it's mine now.

1188
02:03:36,451 --> 02:03:37,785
Are you mad?

1189
02:03:46,086 --> 02:03:48,921
Go! Get out!

1190
02:03:54,636 --> 02:03:58,723
Cissy, put the boys in the cellar.

1191
02:03:58,890 --> 02:04:04,270
I want to have a little conversation
with this one, girl-to-girl.

1192
02:04:13,321 --> 02:04:16,407
What are we gonna do?
We can't leave Hermione alone with her.

1193
02:04:16,575 --> 02:04:17,950
Ron?

1194
02:04:23,165 --> 02:04:24,707
Harry?

1195
02:04:30,422 --> 02:04:32,006
Luna?

1196
02:04:32,591 --> 02:04:36,761
That sword is meant to be in my vault
at Gringotts. How did you get it?

1197
02:04:36,928 --> 02:04:40,056
What else did you and your friends take
from my vault?!

1198
02:04:40,223 --> 02:04:45,603
- I didn't take anything. Please.
- I didn't take anything.

1199
02:04:45,771 --> 02:04:47,313
I don't believe it.

1200
02:04:52,861 --> 02:04:53,986
We have to do something.

1201
02:04:54,154 --> 02:04:58,199
There's no way out of here.
We've tried everything. It's enchanted.

1202
02:04:58,366 --> 02:05:01,035
- Please! please!
- Shut up!

1203
02:05:01,203 --> 02:05:03,037
You're bleeding, Harry.

1204
02:05:03,205 --> 02:05:05,206
That's a curious thing
to keep in your sock.

1205
02:05:14,466 --> 02:05:15,591
Help us.

1206
02:05:21,389 --> 02:05:23,265
- Let her go.
- Shut up. Get back.

1207
02:05:24,601 --> 02:05:28,813
You, goblin, come with me.

1208
02:05:48,458 --> 02:05:49,959
- Aah!
- Dobby?

1209
02:05:50,836 --> 02:05:52,253
What are you doing here?

1210
02:05:52,420 --> 02:05:54,672
Dobby has come to rescue
Harry Potter, of course.

1211
02:05:54,840 --> 02:05:57,299
Dobby will always be there
for Harry Potter.

1212
02:05:57,467 --> 02:06:01,095
You can Apparate in and out of this room?
Could you take us with you?

1213
02:06:01,263 --> 02:06:03,013
Of course, sir. I'm an elf.

1214
02:06:03,807 --> 02:06:05,683
Works for me.

1215
02:06:05,934 --> 02:06:08,269
Dobby, I want you to take Luna
and Mr. Ollivander...

1216
02:06:08,436 --> 02:06:10,896
Shell Cottage
on the outskirts of Tinworth.

1217
02:06:11,273 --> 02:06:12,273
Trust me.

1218
02:06:13,108 --> 02:06:14,525
Whenever you're ready, sir.

1219
02:06:15,235 --> 02:06:17,945
Sir? I like her very much.

1220
02:06:22,868 --> 02:06:26,162
Meet me at the top of the stairs
in 10 seconds.

1221
02:06:35,255 --> 02:06:37,006
Ow.

1222
02:06:42,429 --> 02:06:44,638
Who gets his wand?

1223
02:06:47,392 --> 02:06:51,395
I'm only going to
ask you once more, goblin.

1224
02:06:51,563 --> 02:06:54,982
Think very, very carefully
before you answer.

1225
02:06:55,317 --> 02:06:56,901
I don't know.

1226
02:06:57,068 --> 02:07:00,279
You don't know?
Why weren't you doing your job?

1227
02:07:00,447 --> 02:07:03,657
Who got into my vault?

1228
02:07:04,951 --> 02:07:09,371
Who stole it? Who stole it? Well?

1229
02:07:09,539 --> 02:07:13,584
When I was last in your vault,
the sword was there.

1230
02:07:16,338 --> 02:07:19,548
Oh, well, then perhaps
it just walked out on its own then.

1231
02:07:19,716 --> 02:07:22,176
There is no place safer than Gringotts.

1232
02:07:22,344 --> 02:07:23,719
Liar!

1233
02:07:25,680 --> 02:07:29,099
Consider yourself lucky, goblin.

1234
02:07:31,519 --> 02:07:34,939
The same won't be said for this one.

1235
02:07:35,106 --> 02:07:36,857
Like hell.

1236
02:07:37,609 --> 02:07:38,859
Expelliarmus!

1237
02:07:40,278 --> 02:07:41,362
Stupefy.

1238
02:07:45,533 --> 02:07:46,867
Stop!

1239
02:07:48,036 --> 02:07:49,620
Drop your wands.

1240
02:07:52,499 --> 02:07:53,540
I said, drop them!

1241
02:07:55,043 --> 02:07:56,460
Pick them up, Draco, now.

1242
02:07:57,337 --> 02:07:58,504
Well, well, well...

1243
02:07:59,255 --> 02:08:01,465
...look what we have here.

1244
02:08:03,051 --> 02:08:04,551
It's Harry Potter.

1245
02:08:05,345 --> 02:08:11,725
He's all bright and shiny and new again,
just in time for the Dark Lord.

1246
02:08:11,893 --> 02:08:13,893
Call him.

1247
02:08:54,644 --> 02:08:56,478
Stupefy!

1248
02:08:57,272 --> 02:08:58,939
Stupid elf.

1249
02:08:59,107 --> 02:09:02,151
- You could've killed me.
- Dobby never meant to kill.

1250
02:09:02,318 --> 02:09:06,363
Dobby only meant to maim
or seriously injure.

1251
02:09:08,658 --> 02:09:11,994
How dare you take a witch's wand?

1252
02:09:12,162 --> 02:09:15,164
How dare you defy your masters?

1253
02:09:15,331 --> 02:09:18,459
Dobby has no master.

1254
02:09:18,626 --> 02:09:21,128
Dobby is a free elf.

1255
02:09:21,296 --> 02:09:26,258
And Dobby has come
to save Harry Potter and his friends.

1256
02:09:56,122 --> 02:09:57,790
Hermione.

1257
02:09:57,957 --> 02:10:00,459
You're all right. We're safe.

1258
02:10:00,627 --> 02:10:02,669
We're all safe.

1259
02:10:03,505 --> 02:10:05,714
Harry Potter.

1260
02:10:09,469 --> 02:10:11,303
Dobby.

1261
02:10:21,815 --> 02:10:24,858
Dobby. No, just... Hold on.

1262
02:10:25,026 --> 02:10:29,363
Hold on. Look, just hold on, okay?

1263
02:10:29,531 --> 02:10:31,615
We'll fix you.

1264
02:10:32,033 --> 02:10:34,785
Hermione will have something.

1265
02:10:34,953 --> 02:10:37,287
In your bag. Hermione?

1266
02:10:38,915 --> 02:10:40,249
Hermione?

1267
02:10:42,460 --> 02:10:45,587
What is it? Help me.

1268
02:10:48,174 --> 02:10:51,301
Such a beautiful place...

1269
02:10:53,471 --> 02:10:55,722
...to be with friends.

1270
02:10:57,559 --> 02:11:02,938
Dobby is happy to be with his friend...

1271
02:11:05,358 --> 02:11:07,776
...Harry Potter.

1272
02:11:28,590 --> 02:11:30,966
We should close his eyes.

1273
02:11:31,217 --> 02:11:33,260
Don't you think?

1274
02:11:38,349 --> 02:11:39,766
There.

1275
02:11:40,226 --> 02:11:42,644
Now he could be sleeping.

1276
02:11:57,952 --> 02:12:00,037
I want to bury him.

1277
02:12:01,080 --> 02:12:04,625
Properly. Without magic.

